<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/025075de-66ce-4610-9e92-69d5890bdbc4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Daemon shutdown retracts published LSP diagnostics before exit" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/025075de-66ce-4610-9e92-69d5890bdbc4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/ec530217-8301-41bc-98da-a35b1d9adea7> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/025075de-66ce-4610-9e92-69d5890bdbc4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/025075de-66ce-4610-9e92-69d5890bdbc4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/025075de-66ce-4610-9e92-69d5890bdbc4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "On daemon shutdown, every live Knowledge-LSP session retracts its published diagnostics (publishes an empty set for each open document) before the process exits. Why: publishDiagnostics is sticky client-side — a daemon that dies (dev-cycle SIGTERM restarts happen constantly) leaves squiggles and their hover one-liner alive in the editor with no server behind them to answer textDocument/hover, a misleading half-alive state observed in Zed 2026-07-11 (diagnostic popover shows, dossier hover silently absent until manual language-server restart). This is the shutdown-side completion of the push-surface rule from the push-once diagnostics Lesson (6691839b): a dying publisher must retract what it pushed. Mechanism: spawn_lsp_listener returns an LspListener handle (socket path + live-session registry); main's serve teardown calls shutdown_sessions(), which injects a moosedev/daemonShutdown notification into each session's message loop via a cloned sender on its incoming channel; the session publishes empty diagnostics for its open docs, marks itself retracted, and ends; the flush waits bounded (1s) for retractions plus a 100ms writer-drain grace. Sessions deregister via RAII guard; a session stuck past the timeout is abandoned (its editor keeps stale squiggles — exactly the prior status quo, never worse). Verified by integration test daemon_shutdown_retracts_published_diagnostics plus the full LSP suites." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/025075de-66ce-4610-9e92-69d5890bdbc4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
