<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3ccb78fb-648c-46d6-8b31-230ab0798c3b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3ccb78fb-648c-46d6-8b31-230ab0798c3b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grounded capture is a symbolically gated safety net" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3ccb78fb-648c-46d6-8b31-230ab0798c3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/11e01ea2-f520-4f7c-a165-09532dacd43f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3ccb78fb-648c-46d6-8b31-230ab0798c3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/19df26dc-076b-4339-bee6-bfdc602c13ff> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3ccb78fb-648c-46d6-8b31-230ab0798c3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3ccb78fb-648c-46d6-8b31-230ab0798c3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3ccb78fb-648c-46d6-8b31-230ab0798c3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Grounded capture remains judgment-free about message content and still mints only a proposed ArchitecturalDecision plus queued links for human ratification. Automatic adapters now pass the start of their capture window; before minting, the shared graph layer deterministically abstains when the same author already created an accepted/current typed InformationRecord after that cutoff. This makes the Stop/idle path a safety net for sessions whose primary typed-capture path did not run, without asking an LLM to classify the final message. Claude derives the cutoff from its last successful capture stamp; OpenCode starts at plugin initialization and advances it only after a successful captured-or-abstained result. Both adapters exclude .moosedev/** from capture inputs, so canonical graph churn alone cannot constitute a decision point or perturb the debounce hash. Manual capture calls omit the cutoff and retain the original behavior. Abstentions are recorded as fire telemetry citing the typed record that suppressed capture; no proposal or dense-index write occurs." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3ccb78fb-648c-46d6-8b31-230ab0798c3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3ccb78fb-648c-46d6-8b31-230ab0798c3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/11948738-af62-4a82-a92b-776e32929abf> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3ccb78fb-648c-46d6-8b31-230ab0798c3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-15T00:41:56.873286Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3ccb78fb-648c-46d6-8b31-230ab0798c3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Grounded capture is a symbolically gated safety net" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3ccb78fb-648c-46d6-8b31-230ab0798c3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6255d815-cfb7-412d-9450-1bc9cfe5fa2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d091a06-a6d3-4ca8-9261-d8af349ed900> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d091a06-a6d3-4ca8-9261-d8af349ed900> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Graph import/export page with shared restore core" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d091a06-a6d3-4ca8-9261-d8af349ed900> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex-mcp-client" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d091a06-a6d3-4ca8-9261-d8af349ed900> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Graph import now uses a shared RDF import core exposed through UI, HTTP API, and CLI. The implementation keeps N-Quads as the dataset backup/restore format that preserves project/provenance named graphs, while TTL/N-Triples are single-target graph imports. PATCH inserts only missing quads, REPLACE removes the selected MOOSEDev-owned scope and inserts the parsed import in one transaction, and invalid project imports fail before mutation. The SPARQL UI is now query-only; graph transfer lives on a dedicated Import / Export page with typed RESTORE confirmation for replace mode." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d091a06-a6d3-4ca8-9261-d8af349ed900> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d091a06-a6d3-4ca8-9261-d8af349ed900> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-24T20:02:57.891258Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
