<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d2abe82-3228-4302-a610-7b3983c476f2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/19df26dc-076b-4339-bee6-bfdc602c13ff> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d2abe82-3228-4302-a610-7b3983c476f2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/402e5c0b-dc22-4063-84c6-6b9dd954d540> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d2abe82-3228-4302-a610-7b3983c476f2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d2abe82-3228-4302-a610-7b3983c476f2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d2abe82-3228-4302-a610-7b3983c476f2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: http.addr is only a best-effort hint, and every implicit consumer verifies a direct successful MOOSEDev health response for its own canonical data directory before use. runtime::verify_http_addr disables redirects, requires 2xx, status=ok, the canonical project-graph IRI, and matching canonical data_dir before --status/ui trusts an address. Claude gate/push/capture hooks use curl --fail and the same identity markers. OpenCode journalCheckpoint uses realpathSync.native plus a non-redirecting two-second health preflight before capture. The checked-in ADR generator now applies the same direct identity check before any SPARQL request when its address comes from .moosedev/http.addr; an explicit --addr remains a deliberate operator override. File hygiene invalidates before bootstrap/startup, rewrites after bind, and removes on Axum termination/clean shutdown; in-process workbench publication is clearable and withdrawn with its exact serving task. Behavioral loopback tests prove matching versus mismatched OpenCode capture, matching versus mismatched/redirected ADR discovery, and direct-success/mismatch/non-2xx/redirect Rust verification." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d2abe82-3228-4302-a610-7b3983c476f2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d2abe82-3228-4302-a610-7b3983c476f2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0d25bc07-20ff-4911-8fa3-03692d146dce> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d2abe82-3228-4302-a610-7b3983c476f2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-19T17:26:31.631016Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d2abe82-3228-4302-a610-7b3983c476f2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Implicit HTTP discovery is project-identity verified end to end" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3d2abe82-3228-4302-a610-7b3983c476f2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f9c0c12e-1443-4a8c-82ce-9b7a3104bd6d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3e69bae9-fe9c-44fd-8882-a4b1ae8c78ad> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3e69bae9-fe9c-44fd-8882-a4b1ae8c78ad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Push delivery built and mechanically validated, value unproven" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3e69bae9-fe9c-44fd-8882-a4b1ae8c78ad> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3e69bae9-fe9c-44fd-8882-a4b1ae8c78ad> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Corrected status of the push mechanism. BUILT + MECHANICALLY VALIDATED: the opencode plugin (.opencode/plugins/moosedev-push.ts) loads in headless `opencode run` (from the project CWD, not --dir), all hooks fire (tool.execute.after, experimental.chat.system.transform/messages.transform), MOOSEDEV_DATA_DIR resolves, and after four fixes — symbol-keyed retrieval (records are indexed by symbol e.g. SchemaTriple, not file path), per-turn injection (cross-turn IRI dedup wrongly let an auxiliary hook call consume the record before the real turn), session-set aggregation (opencode passes a different sessionID than tool.execute.after sees), and noise-filter + round-robin per-symbol retrieval — it injects the correct rank-1 record into the model's system prompt (confirmed reaching the prompt 40–52x; offline-verified the cache-gap lesson lands rank-1). VALUE UNPROVEN: on the execution-heavy cache-gap task, delivery is irrelevant because local models hit an execution ceiling (Lesson 5a0e66fe) — they never make the cross-module edits even with the lesson in-prompt (oracle) and even dense-27b+thinking. Push/pull value for local models must therefore be tested on RECALL/Q&A + simple single-edit tasks within local execution capability (pending: whynot_tlo_merge). Push remains sound in principle per invariant #1 (the symbolic layer injects rather than relying on the LLM to pull), but is NOT yet shown to deliver measurable value. Extends value-benchmark AD 47f3f038 / opencode-driver AD f45cf655." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3e69bae9-fe9c-44fd-8882-a4b1ae8c78ad> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3e69bae9-fe9c-44fd-8882-a4b1ae8c78ad> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7a911f2e-d44b-4ec3-92b6-6ee696119fac> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3e69bae9-fe9c-44fd-8882-a4b1ae8c78ad> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T05:00:12.319849Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3e69bae9-fe9c-44fd-8882-a4b1ae8c78ad> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Push delivery (opencode plugin) is built and MECHANICALLY validated; its VALUE for local models is unproven — execution ceiling on code tasks, pending on recall tasks" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3e69bae9-fe9c-44fd-8882-a4b1ae8c78ad> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/12af039b-1e77-47ce-97d9-0880a38f9cb1> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/411161e1-0294-4ea2-93c0-b78c097fef8b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/411161e1-0294-4ea2-93c0-b78c097fef8b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Python substrate support: canonicalized module markers, py+pyi full ladder" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/411161e1-0294-4ea2-93c0-b78c097fef8b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/411161e1-0294-4ea2-93c0-b78c097fef8b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: Python support is the full honest-degradation ladder — a scip-python producer plus a tree-sitter-python fallback covering both .py and .pyi — with scip-python's module idiom canonicalized at ingest. Realizes AD 45f39df4 via AD 256e5702's mechanism. Detection: root markers pyproject.toml / setup.py / setup.cfg / requirements.txt; first-sorted-subdir scan accepts only the strong markers (tooling-only requirements.txt like moosedev's bench/requirements.txt must not spawn scip-python). Command mirrors scip-typescript: npx --yes @sourcegraph/scip-python index --output <tmp>, cwd = project dir, env override MOOSEDEV_SCIP_PYTHON; no --project-name (Constraint 00b3986e elides the git-revision version). Module markers: scip-python renders a module definition as a trailing Meta descriptor (`pkg.mod`/__init__:); ingest rewrites it to the standard namespace module symbol (`pkg.mod`/) via the lang::python canonical_symbol hook, so module classification, display naming (module mints as \"pkg.mod\", never \"__init__\"), logical paths, and the batch-mint module gate all work with zero Python-specific handling downstream — verified live: mint dry-run now creates Module scratch.app. Real __init__ methods/functions are Method descriptors and are never rewritten; a marker with no namespace ancestor is left untouched. Visibility: public ⇔ non-local ∧ top-level ∧ no leading underscore (PEP 8; also excludes top-level dunders); modules fail the top-level gate post-canonicalization and mint through the module path; class members stay lazy-mint-only. Signatures: scip-python leaves signature_documentation empty; the fenced-documentation seam (```python) supplies them. Fallback: tree-sitter-python registered for BOTH py and pyi (stubs are valid Python syntax); anchors function_definition/class_definition only; identities ts:python:<path>:<kind>:<name>; verified live (ts:python:tests/fixtures/ts_fallback.pyi:fn:Widget::render, mode tree-sitter). Accepted consequences carry over from the superseded record: unspecified position_encoding / UTF-16-ish columns on non-ASCII lines (same exposure as scip-typescript, aggregate warning covers it), and npx cold-start + pyright-based indexer weight (mitigated by the debounce, per-producer failure isolation, and the MOOSEDEV_SCIP_PYTHON pin)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/411161e1-0294-4ea2-93c0-b78c097fef8b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
