<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4aa634b8-60a2-4efc-af40-e3ce74cbb97c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Month-2 PRIMARY evaluation rule: instrument-damage annotation with symmetric commitment" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4aa634b8-60a2-4efc-af40-e3ce74cbb97c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4aa634b8-60a2-4efc-af40-e3ce74cbb97c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Registered BEFORE any month-2 data exists (ratified by James 2026-08-10). The Jul 24 - Aug 10 engagement-tally window is annotated instrument-damaged (Lesson 1a4e2761: the tidied 0.7.0/0.7.1 tool descriptions collapsed recall consultation ~8-10x on both trial projects), and month-2 PRIMARY engagement numbers are read WITH that annotation: a low August tally cannot, by itself, establish the \"sustained\" low engagement the frozen PRIMARY kill condition requires. SYMMETRIC COMMITMENT (the clause that keeps this honest): if prediction P1 (AD c3aa0e1c — isMotivatedBy recovers to >=50% on new claude-code ArchitecturalDecisions) and prediction P2 (Lesson 1a4e2761 — weekly fire rate recovers materially above the ~2/week post-Jul-24 floor) have NOT recovered by the month-3 readout (~2026-09-24) under the restored instruments (deployed to the moose-trial daemon 2026-08-10T04:22Z), then the low engagement is accepted as REAL and PRIMARY is evaluated on its face — no further mechanism explanations may be introduced for that window. Kill thresholds themselves are unchanged and untouched (Constraint 75b0cf14 stays as frozen); this rule governs only how the contaminated window is read, and it binds in BOTH directions. Companion instrument note: bench/trial_report.py's ABANDON-RISK flag checks a raw latest-month bucket (no proration, single month) — the flag is advisory dashboard output, not the kill decision; no tally-code change lands before the Aug 24 month-2 batch (instrument-freeze discipline), and proration + tally lifecycle filtering + daemon-side consultation telemetry are registered for the post-Aug-24 step-2 release, effective month-3. Operationalizes protocol AD 07415633 for the damaged window." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4aa634b8-60a2-4efc-af40-e3ce74cbb97c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
