<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6255d815-cfb7-412d-9450-1bc9cfe5fa2a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: v2.2 grounded capture (graph::capture_decision_point; MCP capture_decision_point tool; HTTP POST /api/v1/capture) mints a PROPOSED ArchitecturalDecision whose title is the host's own summary text and whose description carries only diff-derived structural facts (the changed-file list) — extract, never interrogate (AD 145af7e9) — stamped with authorship provenance, and NEVER auto-accepted. Its entity links are queued as v2.1 ProposedLinks rather than written as real edges: one `concerns` proposal per changed file, anchored at the file's module definition (the granularity file-level evidence honestly supports), plus one per caller-identified entity symbol; files or symbols that cannot be anchored in the substrate are reported in the response, never silently dropped. This preserves the D1 interlock by construction: nothing a capture writes can reach a dossier or move the why-coverage numerator before a human ratifies it. isMotivatedBy is link-to-existing only — asserted when the caller names a Requirement that resolves, omitted otherwise, and an unresolvable value fails the whole capture atomically (no orphan record). The ratification queue is generalized behind ProposalKind{Link,Record}: a Record entry is any InformationRecord subclass at lifecycle status proposed (its queue membership IS its status — ProposedLink is not an InformationRecord subclass so link nodes never double-list); accept dispatches Link→link_code materialization, Record→set_status(proposed→accepted); reject flips status for both, preserving the node for audit; resolved records leave the queue view and become ordinary records. pending_count, the LSP nudge, MCP pending_ratifications, GET /proposals, and the workbench inbox all see the union. Capture-noise guards live in the adapters (debounce: opencode 10-min interval at session.idle; Claude Code Stop hook 10-min + change-set-hash stamp), keeping ratification fatigue bounded (spec §6) without policy leaking into adapters — the guards are timing, not judgment." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6255d815-cfb7-412d-9450-1bc9cfe5fa2a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6255d815-cfb7-412d-9450-1bc9cfe5fa2a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-13T15:53:22.422433Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
