<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9756869b-f719-4e9f-8d67-18d0fdfea1d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: the spec §7 acceptance clause \"resolver spot-check ≥95% on a 40-position sample, both modes\" is realized — and hereby ratified — as TWO fixtures: 40 SCIP positions (tests/fixtures/resolver_sample.json, ≥38/40 bar, actual 40/40 at commit 390b4b1) PLUS a separate 10 tree-sitter positions (tests/fixtures/resolver_sample_ts.json, 100% required, mode==TreeSitter asserted), rather than a single 40-position sample mixing both modes. This is the accepted realization of Consequence 5ea1ff19 (\"the acceptance sample must cover both SCIP and tree-sitter resolution\"): both modes are spot-checked on the artifact and the tree-sitter fallback is held to a stricter bar than SCIP. Recorded as a conscious sign-off so the split is not mistaken for a partial reading of the spec." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9756869b-f719-4e9f-8d67-18d0fdfea1d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9756869b-f719-4e9f-8d67-18d0fdfea1d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-13T02:28:41.092873Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9756869b-f719-4e9f-8d67-18d0fdfea1d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "v2.0 \"both modes\" acceptance realized as 40 SCIP + 10 tree-sitter split" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9756869b-f719-4e9f-8d67-18d0fdfea1d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/bfaac061-6b72-4539-aed8-cddbdab4d102> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/97671bfa-f13c-4588-a0fd-f1a3e5c540a1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/97671bfa-f13c-4588-a0fd-f1a3e5c540a1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Shared --serve backend, thin --connect proxies" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/97671bfa-f13c-4588-a0fd-f1a3e5c540a1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/97671bfa-f13c-4588-a0fd-f1a3e5c540a1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The durable KG is RocksDB-backed and single-writer (exclusive lock), so the default per-client stdio model fails when a second MCP client (e.g. Codex beside Claude Code) opens the same project. Decision: one shared backend process (moosedev --serve) owns the store and clients attach as thin --connect proxies over a per-data-dir Unix socket, giving multi-project isolation by construction. Rejected alternatives: per-client stdio servers (cannot share a single locked store); an N-Quads file fallback (loses transactional cache-coherence). Evidence: tasks/todo.md M5." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/97671bfa-f13c-4588-a0fd-f1a3e5c540a1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "deprecated" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/97671bfa-f13c-4588-a0fd-f1a3e5c540a1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/8423e995-ce75-41c8-889c-2fb550708ea2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/97671bfa-f13c-4588-a0fd-f1a3e5c540a1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-18T05:48:08.53293Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/97671bfa-f13c-4588-a0fd-f1a3e5c540a1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Shared --serve backend with thin --connect proxies for concurrent multi-client access" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9918215d-0430-4470-bfba-4fc021b4caa1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9918215d-0430-4470-bfba-4fc021b4caa1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Recall replies budget by priority: prose first, links last, nothing dropped early" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9918215d-0430-4470-bfba-4fc021b4caa1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9918215d-0430-4470-bfba-4fc021b4caa1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: `get_relevant_context` is bounded by ONE budget shared across the returned records, and everything else in the formatter is about spending it in priority order rather than in arrival order.\n\nTHE FAILURE. Server instructions tell agents to call with no `topic` for a broad inventory and `limit` up to 100. Rendering every record whole made exactly that call exceed the MCP response limit: on the dogfood graph at v0.7.0, limit=50 produced 90,712 chars and limit=100 produced 123,699 — an error instead of memory, on the call CLAUDE.md prescribes as recall-first.\n\nNOTHING IS EXEMPT FROM THE BUDGET. Label, kind, and IRI are graph-supplied and unbounded on imported RDF, so each is clipped, and clipped against the RECORD'S SHARE rather than a fixed maximum: at `limit: 100` the share is 400 bytes while fixed caps allowed ~900, so identity alone could carry the reply past the ceiling. A bound that holds only for well-shaped data is not a bound.\n\nTRUNCATION MUST BE REACHABLE. Rendering reserves the framing — key, newline, and the exact truncation marker — BEFORE clipping, so a shortened line fits the room it was granted. Clipping to the full room and appending the marker afterwards pushed every truncated line back over budget, so it was dropped and the value vanished entirely.\n\nPRIORITY, NOT ARRIVAL ORDER. Properties are sorted by `property_rank`: narrative fields (description, rationale) first, then other literals, then IRIs, ascending by size within each. The SAME order governs both passes. Two weaker designs failed first: a fair share alone cannot help a description behind ~166 other properties, since the per-value floor exhausts the budget regardless of how the remainder is divided; and merely grouping prose before links still let an 80KB literal defer alongside a 3KB description and consume the second pass ahead of it. Naming the narrative fields is a deliberate layering compromise — which field carries the meaning is a fact about the ontology, not something a byte budget can derive.\n\nTWO PASSES, NOTHING DISCARDED EARLY. Pass one GATES on a fair share of what remains: values that fit whole are rendered, larger ones defer rather than being clipped to a share that was only provisional. A predicate's values past the third also defer, so one repeated relation cannot crowd out the others. Pass two spends whatever the share still holds, in the same priority order. A value is omitted only when even a floor-length lead will not fit.\n\nHONESTY. Shortening is never silent: the reply reports how many values were truncated and how many not shown, and names the routes to full text. Each record's IRI is always emitted, because it is how the caller reads back what was left out.\n\nMEASURED, same graph: limit=10 → 7,173 chars, limit=50 → 28,989, limit=100 → 26,319. Sharpens Lesson aec883f5: the 100 cap was never the only reason a list-all is not a complete read." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9918215d-0430-4470-bfba-4fc021b4caa1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9918215d-0430-4470-bfba-4fc021b4caa1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bcfefed1-e3c3-4030-80d6-cd70a1d3a2fe> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
