<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a726d76b-36f4-4612-8dd0-a1ccf369179c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a726d76b-36f4-4612-8dd0-a1ccf369179c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: the active-agency policy engine is src/policy/ — free functions over &AppState (evaluate pure; evaluate_and_fire adds best-effort telemetry), mirroring the graph::* convention, because HTTP/LSP/MCP are thin adapters over one Arc<AppState> with no service layer to thread through. Input: a typed PolicyEvent (EntityTouched{file,line?,col?} for PUSH, EditProposed{file,line?,col?,anchor?} for GATE, DecisionPoint{files,summary?} for CAPTURE). Output: a typed serde-serialized PolicyDecision (Allow | Inject{dossier_markdown,entities,records} | Warn{diagnostics} | Gate{disposition,reason,records,entities} | CaptureTrigger{spec}) that carries the FULL outcome; each host adapter enacts only what its host supports (Claude Code can deny, opencode may only ask, hosts without prompts degrade gate→warning-note injection) — so policy stays centralized and adapters are pure translators with zero policy (Consequence 0c447d67). host is passed only for fire telemetry. Reachability: one MCP #[tool] evaluate_policy + one axum POST /api/v1/policy, both thin over evaluate_and_fire, returning the identical verdict JSON. Push==hover by construction: Inject renders via the same graph::get_entity_dossier + render_markdown the LSP hover and MCP dossier tool use. Edits rarely have a cursor at hook time, so EditProposed accepts an `anchor` (the edit's own old_string) located in the on-disk file to scope the gate to overlapping definitions, falling back to a conservative whole-file scan. The WARN shaping (constraint→information, stale-rationale→hint, §5.4 ceiling) was lifted out of LspSession into policy::entity_diagnostics so it is host-independent; the LSP session is now a thin range/encoding renderer and its diagnostics are behavior-identical (regression-proven). fires.jsonl lands here with its first writers (push-fire, gate-fire in evaluate_and_fire; capture-fire at the capture surfaces), closing the deferral condition AD 365adb90 set: FireEvent{ts,verb,host,entity,decision,records_cited} appended best-effort to .moosedev/fires.jsonl (gitignored; telemetry outside the KG per AD 305f87a8; distinct from the in-graph [trial-fire] records, which are untouched). Transport deviation from the spec letter recorded consciously: the Claude Code shell hooks call the daemon over HTTP (.moosedev/http.addr + curl) rather than the moosedev --connect stdio proxy — a bidirectional JSON-RPC session is fragile in bash, and both surfaces are thin over the same evaluate_and_fire, so verdict and fires are identical; the opencode plugin (long-lived Node process) keeps the --connect MCP transport." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a726d76b-36f4-4612-8dd0-a1ccf369179c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
