<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8f95059-d47d-41be-b5f9-6011a9ccad37> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8f95059-d47d-41be-b5f9-6011a9ccad37> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Not-indexed replies discriminate at the MCP handler layer; the editor surface stays silent" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8f95059-d47d-41be-b5f9-6011a9ccad37> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/4f656501-e57e-4ec3-a518-57a482255172> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8f95059-d47d-41be-b5f9-6011a9ccad37> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8f95059-d47d-41be-b5f9-6011a9ccad37> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/accf4f9f-6309-4d3f-8705-26e551824eb0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8f95059-d47d-41be-b5f9-6011a9ccad37> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "phase7-acceptance" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8f95059-d47d-41be-b5f9-6011a9ccad37> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "For position selectors, get_entity_dossier and link_code distinguish three cases: (1) substrate unavailable — run moosedev index; (2) file not anchorable (no SCIP document covers it and no syntactic grammar applies) — the reply names each indexed producer with its document count via one shared Substrate::describe_coverage, so agents can tell a coverage gap from a miss; (3) anchorable but nothing linked — the plain no-recorded-knowledge reply. Dossier replies stay tool_ok (they are answers, not failures); link_code keeps its miss on the error channel. The discrimination lives ONLY in the MCP handler layer: graph::get_entity_dossier still collapses all misses to None, which is what keeps LSP hover and diagnostics silent for uncovered files — the editor surface never explains itself (spec)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8f95059-d47d-41be-b5f9-6011a9ccad37> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8f95059-d47d-41be-b5f9-6011a9ccad37> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-11T00:12:50.398325Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8f95059-d47d-41be-b5f9-6011a9ccad37> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Not-indexed replies discriminate at the MCP handler layer; the editor surface stays silent" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8f95059-d47d-41be-b5f9-6011a9ccad37> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/8c3119b2-300e-4c58-8f98-6c20db6fa4a9> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8f95059-d47d-41be-b5f9-6011a9ccad37> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/9a820e67-5a81-46fc-9b07-7c35e054f822> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8feed19-b4c7-4844-a9db-9102c692680b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8feed19-b4c7-4844-a9db-9102c692680b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LLM fallback stays opt-in via the env dial; host policy is Allowed" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8feed19-b4c7-4844-a9db-9102c692680b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/41084fa1-0359-46b5-8d46-a7e33f9a8121> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8feed19-b4c7-4844-a9db-9102c692680b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/d7ba635f-b5df-4d12-8dd1-a04cacf35078> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8feed19-b4c7-4844-a9db-9102c692680b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8feed19-b4c7-4844-a9db-9102c692680b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "phase7-acceptance" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8feed19-b4c7-4844-a9db-9102c692680b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "When moose collapsed the LLM assist dial from six levels (0-5) to three (PureSymbolic / Sensor / SensorWithFallback) and added a required EngineConfig::fallback_policy host veto, MOOSEDev set fallback_policy to Allowed and kept MOOSEDEV_LLM_ASSIST_LEVEL as the single user-facing control (legacy numerics 3-5 accepted via LlmAssistLevel::from_u8 for one release). The default level remains Sensor, so the epistemically degraded fallback answerer never fires unless a user explicitly dials to 2 (or legacy 5). The gated LLM predicate tiebreak in link suggestion, previously enabled at legacy levels 4-5, now fires only at SensorWithFallback, preserving its default-off symbolic-first behavior." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8feed19-b4c7-4844-a9db-9102c692680b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8feed19-b4c7-4844-a9db-9102c692680b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-11T06:58:57.916335Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8feed19-b4c7-4844-a9db-9102c692680b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "LLM fallback stays opt-in via the env dial; host policy is Allowed" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a8feed19-b4c7-4844-a9db-9102c692680b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/2f44573b-ac64-4307-8be3-818cc80ff2c6> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a97f14e9-e5c2-4113-84f7-be93003ed53b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a97f14e9-e5c2-4113-84f7-be93003ed53b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Editor-slice review hardening: live workbench address, per-folder VS Code clients, explicit eglot entry point" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a97f14e9-e5c2-4113-84f7-be93003ed53b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/11e01ea2-f520-4f7c-a165-09532dacd43f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a97f14e9-e5c2-4113-84f7-be93003ed53b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a97f14e9-e5c2-4113-84f7-be93003ed53b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a97f14e9-e5c2-4113-84f7-be93003ed53b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: four review findings against the editor-expansion slice are fixed at their root, amending sub-claims of ADs 20145567 (openEntity) and d699f118 (thin clients) while their core decisions stand. (1) Workbench URLs no longer trust the on-disk http.addr file — it lingers after a crash, so an HTTP-disabled or bind-failed restart could send window/showDocument to a dead port or an unrelated local service. spawn_http_if_enabled now publishes the bound address into AppState (OnceLock) and workbench_record_url reads ONLY that in-process value: unset means honestly \"workbench not serving\" for openEntity, codeDescription links, and dossier summaries alike; the file remains solely for cross-process --status/ui discovery. (2) The VS Code extension runs one LanguageClient per .moosedev workspace folder (documentSelector scoped to the folder's path glob, workspaceFolder set, per-folder configuration scope), so multi-root workspaces route each file to its own root's daemon instead of leaking every file to the first daemon; folder add/remove events start/stop the matching client. (3) The eglot integration is an explicit `M-x moosedev-eglot` command instead of a global eglot-server-programs entry: a mode-keyed entry is shadowed by the built-in per-language entries, would launch MOOSEDev in projects without a .moosedev root, and `C-u M-x eglot` prompts for a raw command that bypasses initializationOptions. The command root-gates on .moosedev (user-error otherwise) and let-binds a single-entry registry so eglot's own guess resolves to MOOSEDev with its options. (4) `moosedev init --vscode` treats an unparseable .vscode/settings.json as JSONC (comments/trailing commas are valid there): the file is SKIPPED with an explanatory note instead of aborting the whole init run, and is never rewritten (strict merging cannot preserve comments). Verified: init unit tests (29 incl. the JSONC-skip case), lsp_open_entity/dossier/lsp_hover suites on the in-process address, elisp byte-compile plus a live moosedev-eglot batch session (root-gating + dossier hover PASS), VS Code typecheck/bundle, and the Neovim conformance suite." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a97f14e9-e5c2-4113-84f7-be93003ed53b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a97f14e9-e5c2-4113-84f7-be93003ed53b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-19T14:58:48.877824Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
