<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b6df1bf9-d418-4407-8eb9-2813273f65f9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b6df1bf9-d418-4407-8eb9-2813273f65f9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why-coverage denominator is the substrate public surface (is_public not in the graph)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b6df1bf9-d418-4407-8eb9-2813273f65f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/accf4f9f-6309-4d3f-8705-26e551824eb0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b6df1bf9-d418-4407-8eb9-2813273f65f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b6df1bf9-d418-4407-8eb9-2813273f65f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: the v2.1 why-coverage metric's denominator is the substrate's public, non-module, non-test definitions — is_debt_surface(def) = def.is_public && !def.is_module && !is_test_path(def.file) — mapped to a SystemComponent by path (best_component_for_path on definedInPath). This is forced by a hard fact: is_public is NOT persisted on the graph CodeEntity (code_entities.rs writes only hasSubstrateSymbol/hasEntityKind/hasCodeName/hasLogicalPath/definedInPath); it lives solely on the substrate DefinitionEntry (resolver.rs, definition_is_public). Graph code:realizes edges cover only MINTED entities (public + modules batch-minted, private lazily) and carry no visibility, so they cannot express \"the public surface\" — the substrate must drive the denominator. The numerator reuses direct_records_for_entity (the SAME oracle the dossier and hover use), so the metric counts exactly what a human sees on hover and proposed links (which assert no real edge) never inflate it. Load-bearing invariant: is_debt_surface is SHARED VERBATIM by the metric (src/graph/debt.rs) and the LSP code-lens hotspot (src/lsp/mod.rs) so the debt number and the in-editor \"no linked rationale\" flag can never disagree. Components with no public surface report 0/0 (coverage null = \"nothing to document\", not \"fully covered\"); public defs mapping to no component are reported in an explicit unmapped bucket, never charged to a component. This is the objective, role-independent debt number; v2.2 adds a role-weighted view atop it (additive). Implemented v2.1: src/graph/debt.rs, served at GET /api/v1/debt." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b6df1bf9-d418-4407-8eb9-2813273f65f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b6df1bf9-d418-4407-8eb9-2813273f65f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-13T05:30:59.726185Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b6df1bf9-d418-4407-8eb9-2813273f65f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Why-coverage denominator is the substrate public surface (is_public not in the graph)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b72be9f8-c11c-4b80-89ad-375a559a9c1c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b72be9f8-c11c-4b80-89ad-375a559a9c1c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Path→SystemComponent map lives in the graph, not a config file" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b72be9f8-c11c-4b80-89ad-375a559a9c1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/11e01ea2-f520-4f7c-a165-09532dacd43f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b72be9f8-c11c-4b80-89ad-375a559a9c1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b72be9f8-c11c-4b80-89ad-375a559a9c1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: the path→SystemComponent map (the v1 deliverable from Consequence 54937887, needed by capture-time concerns minting and the v2 resolver's realizes inference) is stored IN the project graph as path-glob literals on SystemComponent records — via a new datatype property (working name hasPathGlob) minted through align_concepts at implementation — not as a config file under .moosedev/. Why: the map IS project knowledge (invariant #2 — structured knowledge over free text); in-graph it is captured, superseded, and audited with the existing tools, travels in kg.nq with the code, and is readable by every surface through the one query layer (Constraint 2ba76439 — no second brain). Repo exploration 2026-07-06 confirmed .moosedev/ is a pure runtime data dir (kg.nq + derived caches + socket/pid files) with no config machinery to extend; config today is env-var driven. Spec: spec/MOOSEDev_v2_spec.md §3.6." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b72be9f8-c11c-4b80-89ad-375a559a9c1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b72be9f8-c11c-4b80-89ad-375a559a9c1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-07T04:49:59.908258Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
