<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cabb417d-abcc-4746-ae79-2ceef005ee0b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cabb417d-abcc-4746-ae79-2ceef005ee0b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: the editor expansion remains thin and project-scoped, with lifecycle state represented honestly. Workbench URLs use only an in-process RwLock<Option<SocketAddr>>: the address is published after the HTTP bind succeeds and conditionally withdrawn if that exact Axum server stops, so LSP openEntity, diagnostics, and dossier summaries never advertise a retired listener and never read the crash-stale http.addr hint. VS Code still runs one folder-scoped LanguageClient per .moosedev workspace, but per-folder lifecycle queues now keep an in-flight client visible before awaiting start(), eagerly register all multi-root starts, serialize stop/restart behind startup, prevent activate-time startup from advancing after deactivation, and await failed-client disposal. The explicit root-gated Eglot entry point, Neovim workspace_required guard, RelativePattern folder selector, and JSONC-safe init skip remain unchanged." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cabb417d-abcc-4746-ae79-2ceef005ee0b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
