<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cb68b4de-5e9c-468c-b7d1-4f143c24c7cd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b04ed48c-f395-4c37-9070-a5a9d88cb4c0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cb68b4de-5e9c-468c-b7d1-4f143c24c7cd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/4ae630f1-3297-42da-9fe1-53a25668f94f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cb68b4de-5e9c-468c-b7d1-4f143c24c7cd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/84784849-70a0-4c57-bcfb-5dfd305bc75d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cbdd5f56-8320-4612-b6ed-d5c8fc07d1c6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cbdd5f56-8320-4612-b6ed-d5c8fc07d1c6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Recall replies are bounded by budget alone; the predicate rule is fairness" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cbdd5f56-8320-4612-b6ed-d5c8fc07d1c6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cbdd5f56-8320-4612-b6ed-d5c8fc07d1c6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: `get_relevant_context` is bounded by ONE thing — a character budget shared across the returned records — and every other rule in the formatter exists to spend that budget well, not to impose limits of its own.\n\nTHE FAILURE. Server instructions tell agents to call `get_relevant_context` with no `topic` for a broad inventory and `limit` up to 100. Rendering every record whole made exactly that call exceed the MCP response limit: on the dogfood graph at v0.7.0, limit=50 produced 90,712 chars and limit=100 produced 123,699, so the agent got an error instead of its memory on the call CLAUDE.md prescribes as recall-first.\n\nTHE BUDGET. Every byte a record emits is charged against its share (the even split, or a floor at large `limit`). Nothing is exempt: label, kind, and IRI are all graph-supplied and unbounded on imported RDF, so each is clipped. Charging them without clipping them left a ceiling that held only for well-shaped data, which is not a ceiling.\n\nTRUNCATION MUST BE REACHABLE. Rendering reserves the framing — key, newline, and the exact truncation marker — BEFORE clipping, so a shortened line fits the room it was granted. Clipping to the full room and appending the marker afterwards pushed every truncated line back over budget, so it was dropped and the value vanished. A value is omitted only when even a floor-length lead will not fit. Budgets are byte counts while a `String` splits only on char boundaries, so clipping walks back to the nearest one.\n\nTHE PREDICATE RULE IS FAIRNESS, NOT A CAP. A record's properties arrive in arbitrary order, so a hub carrying ~70 `isConcernedBy` IRIs could consume the record's whole share before its description was reached. The first pass therefore renders at most three values per predicate and DEFERS the surplus; a second pass then spends whatever the share still holds on that surplus in original order. Prose is protected without a link list being truncated at three while the budget sits unused — `coversPath` and `weighs` values are knowledge, not noise.\n\nHONESTY. Shortening is never silent: the reply states how many values were truncated and how many were not shown, and names the routes to full text (narrow `topic`, lower `limit`, or `sparql`). Each record's IRI is always emitted, because it is how the caller reads back what was left out. This makes the shallow-browse rung of the get_relevant_context → query → sparql ladder (AD ee900bdb) explicit in its own output.\n\nMEASURED, same graph: limit=10 → 7,173 chars, limit=50 → 28,989, limit=100 → 26,319. Sharpens Lesson aec883f5 (the 100 cap; use sparql for complete reads) — the cap was never the only reason a list-all is not a complete read, and now the reply says so itself." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cbdd5f56-8320-4612-b6ed-d5c8fc07d1c6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
