<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/df23de4e-800e-4ae6-a170-f17d3b435692> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/df23de4e-800e-4ae6-a170-f17d3b435692> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "0.7.1 makes the mint gap visible; automation deferred" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/df23de4e-800e-4ae6-a170-f17d3b435692> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/df23de4e-800e-4ae6-a170-f17d3b435692> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/accf4f9f-6309-4d3f-8705-26e551824eb0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/df23de4e-800e-4ae6-a170-f17d3b435692> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/df23de4e-800e-4ae6-a170-f17d3b435692> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: 0.7.1 answers Requirement a0581252 with VISIBILITY only — three surfaces now say when a store has an indexed substrate and no CodeEntity records — while automatic minting stays open, because automating it changes when MOOSEDev writes to the graph and that is a design decision, not a patch.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. A `has_any_code_entities` existence probe (deliberately NOT `entities_by_symbol`, which materializes every entity into a BTreeMap and already sits on the per-hover path), wired to the three places the failure was actually experienced: (1) daemon startup logs a warning naming the definition count and the fix; (2) `get_entity_dossier` gains the missing rung in its degradation ladder, checked BEFORE the position-specific rungs because store-wide emptiness applies equally to the `symbol` and `iri` selectors, which previously got no substrate diagnostics at all; (3) LSP hover returns a one-line setup notice instead of nothing. All three share one message constant so they cannot drift.\n\nSILENCE-RULE SCOPE. The hover notice fires ONLY when the store has zero CodeEntities store-wide. Surfacing it per unminted symbol would put a popup on every identifier in the file and break AD 8f20452a; the store-wide case is a configuration error, not knowledge, and is what an editor should report.\n\nVERIFIED 2026-08-04 by reconstructing the trial-store condition (moose-trial's real 64,101-definition substrate against an empty graph): startup warned, all three selectors returned the diagnostic, then `mint --apply` created 5,066 entities and every surface went quiet, the dossier falling back to the correct \"no recorded knowledge is linked\" silence.\n\nWHY NOT AUTOMATE NOW. The daemon owns the RocksDB write lock and the reindex scheduler, so an in-process mint is a contained reuse of `mint_mode`'s body — the objection is not difficulty. It is that auto-mint makes MOOSEDev write CodeEntities and rewrite the committed kg.nq with no human action; at 5,066 entities for moose, doing that on every didSave-debounced generation is constant churn in a version-controlled artifact. That trade belongs in a minor release with the trigger granularity chosen deliberately. Requirement a0581252 stays open.\n\n`moosedev index` is deliberately untouched: it is store-free by design and cannot answer this without taking the write lock." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
