<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dcfd87e8-9ea1-4927-8278-9c1053f5fb0b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Recall-first means list-all, not topic probe" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dcfd87e8-9ea1-4927-8278-9c1053f5fb0b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dcfd87e8-9ea1-4927-8278-9c1053f5fb0b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Before recording into the graph, call get_relevant_context with NO topic (list-all) to see everything already captured. A topic-scoped call returning \"No recorded knowledge relevant to X\" only means nothing cleared the relevance floor (TOPIC_RELEVANCE_FLOOR=0.45) for that wording — it is NOT evidence the graph is empty. During the M4 bootstrap dry-run I concluded the graph was empty from a topic-scoped probe and recorded two records that duplicated existing knowledge (the M5 shared-backend decision 0d81e237; the don't-index-instance-data lesson 89dc91bd) — the exact failure the bootstrap skill's own Phase 0 warns against. Rule: list-all and confirm a record is genuinely new before record_important_decision; duplicates are costly to undo (retract_decision exists now, but prevention is cheaper). Mirrored in tasks/lessons.md as the human-readable view, but this typed Lesson in the graph is the source of truth (invariant #2)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dcfd87e8-9ea1-4927-8278-9c1053f5fb0b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dcfd87e8-9ea1-4927-8278-9c1053f5fb0b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-18T06:49:17.231111Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dcfd87e8-9ea1-4927-8278-9c1053f5fb0b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Recall-first means a list-all get_relevant_context, not a topic probe" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd4a6240-b50e-45b2-b16d-0cb7e983073a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd4a6240-b50e-45b2-b16d-0cb7e983073a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Enforce the LSP severity ceiling at runtime, not only with debug_assert" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd4a6240-b50e-45b2-b16d-0cb7e983073a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd4a6240-b50e-45b2-b16d-0cb7e983073a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd4a6240-b50e-45b2-b16d-0cb7e983073a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Pattern: the v2.0 \"no diagnostic above Information\" ceiling was guarded in lsp::Session::publish() by `debug_assert!(diagnostics.iter().all(is_allowed_diagnostic_severity))`. debug_assert! is compiled OUT of release, so the shipped binary asserted nothing — the ceiling held only by construction (the LSP happens to construct only INFORMATION and HINT) plus the test-time assert_severity_ceiling. A future change constructing a Warning/Error would have shipped silently past a comment claiming the gate \"cannot emit Warning or Error.\" Discovered during the v2.0 acceptance pass (2026-07-12). Fix: publish() now retains only allowed severities and tracing::warn!s on any drop, so the release artifact enforces the ceiling rather than merely asserting it (debug_assert kept for a loud test-time failure). Rule: a load-bearing runtime invariant needs a real runtime guard (filter/clamp + warn/log); debug_assert documents intent but vanishes in release and must not be the sole enforcement. Corollary for acceptance: grep the construction sites AND exercise the runtime path — a criterion satisfied \"by construction\" can still lack the guard its comment promises." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd4a6240-b50e-45b2-b16d-0cb7e983073a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd4a6240-b50e-45b2-b16d-0cb7e983073a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-13T02:29:03.879343Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd4a6240-b50e-45b2-b16d-0cb7e983073a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Enforce the LSP severity ceiling at runtime, not only with debug_assert" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd5e7d15-54a4-4dee-8f44-6c1198756a9d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd5e7d15-54a4-4dee-8f44-6c1198756a9d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Enrich: record→record edges only, via RDF-1.2 reification" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd5e7d15-54a4-4dee-8f44-6c1198756a9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/11e01ea2-f520-4f7c-a165-09532dacd43f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd5e7d15-54a4-4dee-8f44-6c1198756a9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd5e7d15-54a4-4dee-8f44-6c1198756a9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Two implementation refinements to AD e0b7b528, both confirmed by the dogfood prototype. (1) ENCODING: the inferred-edge provenance tag is RDF 1.2 reification (R rdf:reifies «s p o» ; prov:wasGeneratedBy <activity>), NOT the RDF-star << s p o >>-as-subject the AD describes. The Trivyn oxigraph fork is RDF 1.2 — Term::Triple is admitted only in OBJECT position (oxrdf triple.rs: Quad/Triple subjects are NamedOrBlankNode), and the codebase test-rejects SPARQL UPDATE (tests/sparql.rs) — so the reifier idiom is the ONLY Transaction-API path. It preserves the AD's per-triple-provenance + drop-and-rerun intent (clear_reasoner_inferences recovers inferred triples from reifiers attributed to the GROWL agent). (2) SCOPING: enrich_delta keeps only record→record OBJECT-PROPERTY edges (subject AND object are asserted A-box nodes of kg/project), NOT the full prp-inv/spo/dom-rng/cax-sco closure the AD names. Feeding the whole ontology T-box makes GROWL also emit CCO/BFO T-box closure, datatype-property liftings (record→literal), and rdf:type completions — 882 raw edges on the dogfood graph vs only 69 record→record. The other ~813 are invisible to record_neighbors (it follows only edges whose OBJECT is an InformationRecord), so they add zero retrieval value while bloating storage/export and shifting SHACL targeting. The 69 kept (the bidirectional-walk win): motivates 6, isRationaleFor 21, isSupersededBy 19, isConstrainedBy 2, BFO part-of 21. Code: src/reasoning/mod.rs (enrich_delta abox-subject + object-is-record filters; enrich/enrich_now), src/provenance/mod.rs (reasoner_inference_quads, clear_reasoner_inferences), trigger in src/graph/mod.rs AppState.ensure_enriched. Verified: 3 unit + 1 integration test, 0 new SHACL violations, idempotent." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd5e7d15-54a4-4dee-8f44-6c1198756a9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd5e7d15-54a4-4dee-8f44-6c1198756a9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-22T04:40:22.35549Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
