<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dd5e7d15-54a4-4dee-8f44-6c1198756a9d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e0b7b528-58f9-4638-a0d8-ef4cc6063c6b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/de96fbac-ca2f-4b95-a1be-5536354b2649> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/de96fbac-ca2f-4b95-a1be-5536354b2649> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Temporal bootstrap at scale on trivyn, N=3" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/de96fbac-ca2f-4b95-a1be-5536354b2649> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/de96fbac-ca2f-4b95-a1be-5536354b2649> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Third temporal git-walk bootstrap (after moosedev 78/66/7 Lesson d1b44d5e, and burrow 64/54/4 Lesson 2d79b2d2), now at scale and run overnight. 320 first-parent commits -> 255 decision-bearing episodes (65 mechanical skips), gpt-5.4-mini via the codex backend, resumable. RESULT: 416 nodes (291 ArchitecturalDecision, 47 Rationale, 37 Constraint, 37 Requirement, 2 Lesson, 1 Consequence, 1 SystemComponent); 186 edges (76 isMotivatedBy, 47 hasRationale, 42 supersedes, 16 constrains, 3 concerns, 1 learnedFrom, 1 resultsIn); edge:node 0.45; validate_against_architecture Conforms, 0 violations. TIMELINE (from the store, not the prompt): trivyn's real 2025-07-14 .. 2026-06-18 (~11 months) — correct historical stamping at scale. SUPERSEDE CHAINS: 42, ALL look-back-correct (new.hasTimestamp >= old) across genuinely different historical dates (so look-back correctness is real, not run-order coincidence). Many genuine reversals (OWL reasoning screen added 2025-08 -> retired 2026-05; CodeMirror 6 -> YASQE SPARQL editor; `reasonable` submodule -> `growl` crate; domain hints added 2025-10 -> removed 2026-04 full add-then-remove cycle; free/pro split -> dev/beta/academic editions); ~5-6 are degenerate same-title self-supersedes (capture artifact, as in burrow chain 1) so ~36 genuine. SIGNIFICANCE: (1) temporal bootstrap N=3 generalization at SCALE (~6x burrow/moosedev node count); (2) 42 supersede chains (6x burrow's 4) = rich currency material, far more likely to contain a RANK-INVERTED pair (superseded outranks current in BM25) to demonstrate the structured-currency advantage decisively like moosedev glrc; (3) 416 records + a cold B0 arm + multi-hop tasks should finally surface the efficiency H2/H3 differences burrow was too small for. HONEST CAVEAT: edge:node 0.45 is LOWER than burrow/moosedev (~0.85) — per-episode capture on trivyn's larger diffs skewed to supersedes/isMotivatedBy/hasRationale and produced few concerns/constrains/weighs, so the 291 ADs are loosely linked (fewer multi-hop paths than the node count implies; a capture-skill richness gap worth a nudge). NEXT: (a) efficiency matrix on trivyn-temporal (B0/B1-md/B1-rag/B2 incl. cold + multi-hop); (b) mine the 42 chains for a rank-inverted currency pair. Relates to d1b44d5e, 2d79b2d2, 952b72d1 (cross-corpus currency), c0aa3509 (codex capture); private corpus -> store stays local in ~/.moosedev-stores/trivyn-temporal." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/de96fbac-ca2f-4b95-a1be-5536354b2649> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/de96fbac-ca2f-4b95-a1be-5536354b2649> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-20T11:47:17.13006Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/de96fbac-ca2f-4b95-a1be-5536354b2649> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Temporal bootstrap at SCALE (trivyn, N=3): gpt-5.4-mini/codex captured 416 nodes / 186 edges / 42 look-back-correct supersede chains over trivyn's real 2025-07..2026-06 timeline, 0 violations" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/df808a17-3593-4c1b-9f12-5c28051cc931> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/df808a17-3593-4c1b-9f12-5c28051cc931> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Capability Stage-1 (agentic): structure wins categorically on large-set completeness; efficiency edge modest" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/df808a17-3593-4c1b-9f12-5c28051cc931> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/ce49a867-7ebc-41d5-879c-fa59eed3ae65> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/df808a17-3593-4c1b-9f12-5c28051cc931> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/df808a17-3593-4c1b-9f12-5c28051cc931> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Capability benchmark Stage-1 — AGENTIC confirmation of the Stage-0 tool-ceiling (Lesson 392855d0). trivyn-temporal, codex/gpt-5.4-mini, B0/B1-rag/B2 × 11 graph-derived capability_qa questions, tooluse, graded by grade_set (set recall/precision/F1). Harness: bench/run_capability.sh, grade_set.py, capability_report.py (regrade-safe). RESULT — ACCURACY VERDICT PASSES (pre-registered): pooled over the hard classes (set/negation/multi-hop) B2 F1=0.96, B1-rag F1=0.31, B0=0.00. Per class: set_completeness B2 1.00 (7/7 pass) vs B1-rag 0.28 vs B0 0; negation B2 0.97 vs B1-rag 0.54 vs B0 0; supersession B2 0.85 vs B1-rag 0.61 vs B0 0; multi_hop B2 0.67 vs B1-rag 0.00 vs B0 0. THE WIN SCALES WITH UNDERLYING SET SIZE, not the question phrasing: large sets (>=~40) are categorical — neg_accepted_ads_no_motivation (104-absence in 141 ADs): B1-rag made 30 tool calls and got 11/104 (recall 0.11), B2 made 7 calls and got 99/104 (0.95); set_all_constraints (37): B1 7/37, B2 37/37. SMALL sets/single-item lookups TIE — neg_constraints_no_rationale (32-absence in a 37-class) B1-rag 0.91 (listing ~all 37 constraints accidentally covers a 32/37 absence), sup_head_of_reversal (single chain head) both ~1.0. So the categorical advantage is COMPLETENESS OVER LARGE SETS (set-completeness, large-negation, multi-hop traversal) — where flat top-k RAG cannot enumerate — not negation or supersession per se. EFFICIENCY VERDICT = REVIEW (modest, NOT the pre-registered <20%): B2 pooled tot_tok 167.9K vs B1-rag 320.6K = 1.9x (B2 ~52% of B1); tool-calls 2.5-4.8x fewer on set/negation; multi_hop INVERTS (B1 fails fast/cheap at 0.3x B2 tokens). The <20% threshold was over-calibrated on the currency precedent; the honest efficiency edge is ~2x tokens + ~3x fewer tool-calls, SECONDARY to the categorical accuracy win. METHODOLOGY: a grader artifact scored exact-correct B1+B2 prose/scalar chain-head answers as 0.0 (n_predicted=0 -> precision 0 -> F1 0); fixed by flooring n_predicted at matched (extends grading-artifact Lesson a03dbe13). CAVEAT: N=1 per question; negation/supersession/multi_hop have only 1-2 questions each (thin per-class Wilson bars) — the set_completeness sweep (7/7 B2, 0/7 B1) is the robust core. Next: oxigraph-trivyn (neutral/public) generalization." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/df808a17-3593-4c1b-9f12-5c28051cc931> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/df808a17-3593-4c1b-9f12-5c28051cc931> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-23T00:56:26.164047Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/df808a17-3593-4c1b-9f12-5c28051cc931> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Capability Stage-1 (agentic): structure wins categorically on large-set completeness; efficiency edge modest" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/df808a17-3593-4c1b-9f12-5c28051cc931> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/47f3f038-8fd7-4a96-9c74-15a24bf8be17> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/df808a17-3593-4c1b-9f12-5c28051cc931> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7b824b26-36bb-47ce-a235-0a4fdf31a662> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dff41e50-992c-4078-ac38-336884117cf5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dff41e50-992c-4078-ac38-336884117cf5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A verification verdict needs a sentinel: exit code AND run-completed proof" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dff41e50-992c-4078-ac38-336884117cf5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dff41e50-992c-4078-ac38-336884117cf5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: a verification run is only evidence once you can see BOTH that it finished and what status it finished with. Anything else — a filtered exit code, a partially-written log — reads exactly like success.\n\nTHE SHAPE THAT WORKS. Redirect the whole run to a file and append an explicit sentinel carrying the real status, then refuse to draw any conclusion until the sentinel is present:\n\n  cargo test --no-fail-fast > /tmp/suite.txt 2>&1; echo \"EXIT=$?\" >> /tmp/suite.txt\n  until grep -q EXIT= /tmp/suite.txt; do sleep 15; done\n\nThen read the sentinel, `test result:` lines, and the binary count together. `--no-fail-fast` matters: by default cargo stops at the first failing binary, so a truncated-looking log is ambiguous between \"still running\" and \"aborted on failure\".\n\nTWO WAYS THIS HAS FAILED, BOTH REPORTED AS GREEN.\n(1) FILTERED STATUS. `cargo test | tail -60` (2026-07-09) and `cargo test | grep -E ... > file; echo \"EXIT=$?\"` (2026-08-06) both exit 0 while cargo FAILED, because `$?` belongs to the LAST stage. The second was written after the first was recorded — the banned construct is any filter in the gating position, not the word `tail`.\n(2) MID-FLIGHT READ. On 2026-08-06 the results file was read while the run was in flight; 14 binaries had reported ok and the count was published as a green full suite. The run went on to fail 2 tests in `tests/mcp_replies.rs` — a real regression, found instead by an external code review. A log with no failures in it is not a log of a run with no failures.\n\nPROCESS COROLLARIES. Never treat `pgrep`-style liveness as the completion signal (it gave a false \"not running\" for a live cargo process in the same session); trust the sentinel you wrote. And when reporting, distinguish what was OBSERVED from what was INFERRED — \"312 tests, 0 failures\" asserted a total that had merely not failed *yet*.\n\nComplements Lesson 9a4470ef (scoped by default, full suite at acceptance gates — this governs how that gate is read) and Lesson 6fe1a3bd (verify the artifact, not the checkmark — the same distrust, one layer out)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dff41e50-992c-4078-ac38-336884117cf5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dff41e50-992c-4078-ac38-336884117cf5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e3faf61-58a9-416f-af61-4d9ff634847f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
