<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea6c568d-ef9b-4c43-b091-8bf24ef28a86> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do not infer systematic LSP drift from sparse squiggle locations" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea6c568d-ef9b-4c43-b091-8bf24ef28a86> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea6c568d-ef9b-4c43-b091-8bf24ef28a86> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea6c568d-ef9b-4c43-b091-8bf24ef28a86> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Pattern: squiggles appearing on wrong editor lines do not by themselves prove a saved-file versus active-buffer offset. The exact-line-alignment change was based on that inference, but the user's follow-up observation showed the remaining locations are seemingly random. Rule: before changing position mapping, capture the emitted publishDiagnostics payload and compare each diagnostic's source entity, server range, active-buffer range, and rendered Zed line; require a repeatable transformation before selecting a mapping fix." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
