<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0d25bc07-20ff-4911-8fa3-03692d146dce> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0d25bc07-20ff-4911-8fa3-03692d146dce> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Implicit HTTP discovery is project-identity verified end to end" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0d25bc07-20ff-4911-8fa3-03692d146dce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0d25bc07-20ff-4911-8fa3-03692d146dce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded decision still missed scripts/generate-adrs-from-graph.py, which read http.addr and could query a different MOOSEDev project after stale-port reuse. It also relied on source-string assertions for the adapter identity behavior. The replacement completes the consumer inventory and records executable fake-server evidence for the payload-bearing OpenCode and ADR paths." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0d25bc07-20ff-4911-8fa3-03692d146dce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0d25bc07-20ff-4911-8fa3-03692d146dce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-19T17:26:31.631016Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0d25bc07-20ff-4911-8fa3-03692d146dce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Implicit HTTP discovery is project-identity verified end to end" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0e8c54ea-6782-478e-96b4-99e9889d6082> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0e8c54ea-6782-478e-96b4-99e9889d6082> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Web UI binds ephemeral loopback port; http.addr invalidated on startup" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0e8c54ea-6782-478e-96b4-99e9889d6082> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0e8c54ea-6782-478e-96b4-99e9889d6082> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The original claim \"read from http.addr, trusted only while the backend is live, so a stale file from a crash is ignored\" was false in one scenario: a crashed daemon never removes the file, and when it RESTARTS with HTTP disabled, misconfigured, or failing to bind, the backend IS live — so --status/ui and the generated policy hooks trust the previous run's address, which by then may be a dead port or an unrelated local process that reclaimed it (hooks would POST policy payloads to it). Caught by review 2026-07-19; fixed by invalidating http.addr at the top of every HTTP startup path." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0e8c54ea-6782-478e-96b4-99e9889d6082> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0e8c54ea-6782-478e-96b4-99e9889d6082> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-19T15:15:19.393957Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0e8c54ea-6782-478e-96b4-99e9889d6082> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Web UI binds ephemeral loopback port; http.addr invalidated on startup" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/11948738-af62-4a82-a92b-776e32929abf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/11948738-af62-4a82-a92b-776e32929abf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Grounded capture is a symbolically gated safety net" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/11948738-af62-4a82-a92b-776e32929abf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/11948738-af62-4a82-a92b-776e32929abf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Dogfooding produced repeated file-list and build-status ADR noise even when the session had already recorded deliberate typed knowledge (Lesson b67a4207). Timing and dirty-tree guards alone were insufficient because .moosedev/kg.nq changes on every graph write. The replacement retains content-neutral capture while moving the missing distinction into deterministic graph state." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/11948738-af62-4a82-a92b-776e32929abf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/11948738-af62-4a82-a92b-776e32929abf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-15T00:41:56.873286Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/11948738-af62-4a82-a92b-776e32929abf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Grounded capture is a symbolically gated safety net" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e3faf61-58a9-416f-af61-4d9ff634847f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e3faf61-58a9-416f-af61-4d9ff634847f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: A verification verdict needs a sentinel: exit code AND run-completed proof" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e3faf61-58a9-416f-af61-4d9ff634847f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e3faf61-58a9-416f-af61-4d9ff634847f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The rule as written (\"no tail/head pipelines; check the exit code\") was recorded in July and violated again on 2026-08-06 in a way it did not cover. The gating command was `cargo test 2>&1 | grep -E ... > file; echo \"EXIT=$?\"` — a filter pipeline, so `$?` was grep's status, exactly the banned shape but with `grep` instead of `tail`, and the echoed \"EXIT=0\" then got reported as proof. A SECOND failure mode the old lesson did not name compounded it: the results file was read while cargo was still running, so a partial log of 14 all-ok binaries was reported as a green full suite when the run later failed 2 tests. The prohibition needed to become a positive procedure — write a sentinel AFTER the command and refuse to judge until it appears — because \"don't pipe\" does not tell you a mid-flight file is also untrustworthy." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e3faf61-58a9-416f-af61-4d9ff634847f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e3faf61-58a9-416f-af61-4d9ff634847f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-07T00:03:07.380344Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e3faf61-58a9-416f-af61-4d9ff634847f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: A verification verdict needs a sentinel: exit code AND run-completed proof" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e678ee9-5112-4229-a5a8-095879459af0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e678ee9-5112-4229-a5a8-095879459af0> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Python substrate support: canonicalized module markers, py+pyi full ladder" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e678ee9-5112-4229-a5a8-095879459af0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e678ee9-5112-4229-a5a8-095879459af0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Post-implementation review found two real defects in the first cut: (P1) Python modules were excluded from batch minting — the `pkg/__init__:` Meta marker failed both mint gates (is_module_symbol false at grammar level, is_public false via the underscore gate), so no Python module ever entered the addressable skeleton; and (P2) .pyi stub files were registered with the producer but not with the tree-sitter fallback, so uncovered stubs could not be anchored. The replacement fixes P1 by canonicalizing the marker at ingest instead of special-casing every classifier, and P2 by registering both extensions in the fallback spec." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e678ee9-5112-4229-a5a8-095879459af0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e678ee9-5112-4229-a5a8-095879459af0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-18T22:16:25.554797Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e678ee9-5112-4229-a5a8-095879459af0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Python substrate support: canonicalized module markers, py+pyi full ladder" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2191efb1-edd2-43fb-829c-7e40100c0ae0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2191efb1-edd2-43fb-829c-7e40100c0ae0> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: http.addr is a hint; consumers verify backend identity via /api/v1/health" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2191efb1-edd2-43fb-829c-7e40100c0ae0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2191efb1-edd2-43fb-829c-7e40100c0ae0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The replaced decision claimed \"the file's presence therefore always describes the CURRENT run\" — overclaimed, as review round 3 (2026-07-19) showed: startup invalidation cannot cover the interval while a crashed daemon stays down, nor the window between a restart's launch and its invalidation call (originally placed after the long bootstrap), and nothing withdrew the file when the HTTP task ended mid-run. The gate/push/capture hooks POST edit text and file lists to whatever answers at the published address, so a reclaimed ephemeral port could hand project payloads to an unrelated local process. File hygiene alone cannot close this; consumers must verify who is answering." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2191efb1-edd2-43fb-829c-7e40100c0ae0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2191efb1-edd2-43fb-829c-7e40100c0ae0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-19T15:55:07.55575Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2191efb1-edd2-43fb-829c-7e40100c0ae0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: http.addr is a hint; consumers verify backend identity via /api/v1/health" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2456f9ef-08c6-4f3a-ab94-dd2213df53a6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2456f9ef-08c6-4f3a-ab94-dd2213df53a6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: encode the get_relevant_context→query→sparql precision/cost ladder" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2456f9ef-08c6-4f3a-ab94-dd2213df53a6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2456f9ef-08c6-4f3a-ab94-dd2213df53a6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded requirement coupled a still-valid goal (reliable tool selection / the precision-cost ladder) to a now-reversed prohibition (\"no A-box vector index; get_relevant_context must not be upgraded to vector search\"). The prohibition is superseded by Constraint af5ebd6d, which permits dense as a bounded seed feeding symbolic expansion; the tool-selection work item remains valid and is carried forward here." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2456f9ef-08c6-4f3a-ab94-dd2213df53a6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2456f9ef-08c6-4f3a-ab94-dd2213df53a6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-21T07:26:00.337169Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2456f9ef-08c6-4f3a-ab94-dd2213df53a6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Encode the get_relevant_context → query → sparql precision/cost ladder in tool-selection guidance (A-box dense seed now permitted)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/262a87b8-8a96-49be-bb11-4fdcbe22fb1a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/262a87b8-8a96-49be-bb11-4fdcbe22fb1a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: no A-box index, precision via walks" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/262a87b8-8a96-49be-bb11-4fdcbe22fb1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/262a87b8-8a96-49be-bb11-4fdcbe22fb1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded Constraint framed the absence of A-box semantic similarity as a gap with a sanctioned workaround (embed instance text in moosedev via the backbone). That is misleading: not indexing instances is a deliberate MOOSE design choice — walk planning was devised to avoid the vector-index/RAG trap and yield more precise, auditable retrieval. The proposed \"workaround\" is an anti-pattern, not a gap to fill." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/262a87b8-8a96-49be-bb11-4fdcbe22fb1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/262a87b8-8a96-49be-bb11-4fdcbe22fb1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-18T04:57:07.675692Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/262a87b8-8a96-49be-bb11-4fdcbe22fb1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: MOOSE deliberately does not index instance (A-box) data; precision comes from walk planning" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/280c1722-9f41-4488-954c-333bec2c56ca> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/280c1722-9f41-4488-954c-333bec2c56ca> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: benchmark model suite spans the capability spectrum" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/280c1722-9f41-4488-954c-333bec2c56ca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/280c1722-9f41-4488-954c-333bec2c56ca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Extends the opencode-only harness decision: testing the v1 thesis (memory = efficiency at the frontier, capability for weak models) requires spanning model families and capability tiers, which no single harness hosts cleanly. Claude Code headless (claude -p) natively runs and token-accounts Claude models via --output-format json, so opencode is no longer the sole driver. The symmetric memory-as-MCP-server principle is retained." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/280c1722-9f41-4488-954c-333bec2c56ca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/280c1722-9f41-4488-954c-333bec2c56ca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T18:00:02.317673Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/280c1722-9f41-4488-954c-333bec2c56ca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Benchmark model suite spans the capability spectrum (codex-spark / Sonnet / Haiku / A3B), run per-harness; within-model token-ratio is the efficiency metric" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/29297125-b214-4e7d-99ee-beb938c15e98> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/29297125-b214-4e7d-99ee-beb938c15e98> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Phase-2 turf (corrected): B2 ties mem0 on relevance + currency, wins completeness" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/29297125-b214-4e7d-99ee-beb938c15e98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/29297125-b214-4e7d-99ee-beb938c15e98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The original turf result said \"mem0 wins simple relevance (B2 thrashes)\", but that was confounded by a dead-MCP harness bug (Lesson 0a890ea9): a broken MOOSEDEV_BIN meant get_relevant_context never launched, so B2's agent fell back to grepping the store (0.5-1.2M tokens). After fixing the bin, gpt-5.4-mini calls get_relevant_context 4/4 at ~35k tokens (cov 0.82) — B2 TIES mem0 on relevance, it does not lose. The completeness win is unaffected." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/29297125-b214-4e7d-99ee-beb938c15e98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/29297125-b214-4e7d-99ee-beb938c15e98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-23T19:03:27.891068Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/29297125-b214-4e7d-99ee-beb938c15e98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Phase-2 turf (corrected): B2 ties mem0 on relevance + currency, wins completeness" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/29388844-a2a8-49bd-a201-50be51874278> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/29388844-a2a8-49bd-a201-50be51874278> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Recall replies are bounded by budget alone; the predicate rule is fairness" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/29388844-a2a8-49bd-a201-50be51874278> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/29388844-a2a8-49bd-a201-50be51874278> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record described \"two independent caps: per-predicate ... and per-record\", which read as — and was implemented as — discarding a predicate's fourth and later values outright. On a single-record reply with 39KB of the budget unspent that silently dropped real knowledge: a SystemComponent's `coversPath` list, an ArchitecturalDecision's `weighs` edges. The per-predicate rule should only prevent crowding, not impose a ceiling the budget does not require. Also corrects the bound again: `kind` and `iri` were charged to a record's share but never clipped, so a pathological imported IRI could still carry a reply past the response limit — the same \"bounded only for well-shaped data\" gap the labels fix addressed. Both found by code review, 2026-08-06." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/29388844-a2a8-49bd-a201-50be51874278> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/29388844-a2a8-49bd-a201-50be51874278> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-07T03:15:23.449005Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/29388844-a2a8-49bd-a201-50be51874278> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Recall replies are bounded by budget alone; the predicate rule is fairness" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2e88601d-30a7-4443-95ce-c8055827178c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2e88601d-30a7-4443-95ce-c8055827178c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Corrected-grader currency: B2 current, free-text fails at push" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2e88601d-30a7-4443-95ce-c8055827178c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/ce49a867-7ebc-41d5-879c-fa59eed3ae65> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2e88601d-30a7-4443-95ce-c8055827178c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2e88601d-30a7-4443-95ce-c8055827178c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Re-graded all stored currency runs with the negation/markdown-aware grader (no agent re-runs; final_text is logged per row — see Lesson 9fc21dc0 and the reproducible bench/regrade.py). Measuring currency by coverage of the CURRENT markers (robust) instead of the brittle stale-marker substring, the 4-pair result holds on the METRIC, not just hand-read final_text: B2 is 100% current in every cell (25/25 across gpt-5.3-codex-spark, gpt-5.4-mini, gpt-5.5, qwen3.6-a3b and both oracle+tooluse). Free-text (B1-rag) is 100% current on 3 pairs (connect_daemon, ontology, supersede) and collapses only on glrc — the rank-inverted pair where the SUPERSEDED 'pure-symbolic' record outranks the current record in BM25. New mechanistic refinement of abe11031: that collapse is REGIME-DEPENDENT. In ORACLE/push (top-k retrieved chunks injected into the prompt) B1-rag glrc = 1/13 (8%, catastrophic) because the agent is handed the stale top hit and free text has no currency signal to override it; in TOOLUSE (agent runs its own searches) B1-rag glrc recovers to 10/11 (91%) because the agent can dig past the stale top hit. B2 = 100% in BOTH regimes (oracle 13/13, tooluse 12/12). Takeaway: structured current-only retrieval is a GUARANTEE; free-text currency is a content/rank/DELIVERY-regime gamble — worst exactly where push delivery meets BM25 rank-inversion. Refines abe11031; grading basis from Lesson 9fc21dc0; written up in bench/RESULTS.md (human-readable view)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2e88601d-30a7-4443-95ce-c8055827178c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "proposed" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2e88601d-30a7-4443-95ce-c8055827178c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-20T03:53:43.76858Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2e88601d-30a7-4443-95ce-c8055827178c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Corrected-grader currency result: B2 100% current in EVERY cell (25/25, all models × both regimes); free-text's glrc catastrophe is localized to the oracle/push regime (8%) and recovers under tooluse (91%)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/3a45f892-2367-44fa-b0c3-13e0cf841368> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/3a45f892-2367-44fa-b0c3-13e0cf841368> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: retract Decision point: .claude/hooks/moosedev-push.sh, .moosedev/kg.nq, ontologies/software-code.ttl, on…" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/3a45f892-2367-44fa-b0c3-13e0cf841368> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/3a45f892-2367-44fa-b0c3-13e0cf841368> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Mechanical automatic capture recorded a file-list checkpoint after the session's deliberate typed knowledge was already captured. It is redundant inbox noise, not an architectural decision." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/3a45f892-2367-44fa-b0c3-13e0cf841368> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/3a45f892-2367-44fa-b0c3-13e0cf841368> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-15T00:41:11.454717Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/3a45f892-2367-44fa-b0c3-13e0cf841368> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: retract Decision point: .claude/hooks/moosedev-push.sh, .moosedev/kg.nq, ontologies/software-code.ttl, on…" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/509b66b7-42e6-47a3-9e9a-3ae579b65aa2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/509b66b7-42e6-47a3-9e9a-3ae579b65aa2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Scoped verification by default; full suite only at acceptance gates" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/509b66b7-42e6-47a3-9e9a-3ae579b65aa2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/509b66b7-42e6-47a3-9e9a-3ae579b65aa2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "User correction 2026-07-11: \"The tests take FOREVER. necessary to run the full (slow) suite all the time? It's a bottleneck in the workflow.\" The predecessor already banned per-subagent suite runs but still prescribed one full-suite run \"just before commit\" — in practice that made the full suite a per-change tax (~10+ min: cold heavy build plus serialized integration tests that each bootstrap a fresh AppState). The revision moves the full suite from a per-change gate to an explicit acceptance gate." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/509b66b7-42e6-47a3-9e9a-3ae579b65aa2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/509b66b7-42e6-47a3-9e9a-3ae579b65aa2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-11T16:33:18.424544Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/509b66b7-42e6-47a3-9e9a-3ae579b65aa2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Scoped verification by default; full suite only at acceptance gates" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/51338ce8-1662-4fa3-8401-9c72f8f1339b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/51338ce8-1662-4fa3-8401-9c72f8f1339b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: clean currency A/B, structured beats free-text" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/51338ce8-1662-4fa3-8401-9c72f8f1339b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/51338ce8-1662-4fa3-8401-9c72f8f1339b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The earlier currency test was confounded (free-text was made currency-aware via baked-in status, and a no-code framing made agents flail), so it concluded the structured-representation edge \"has not appeared in any test.\" This run removed both confounds exactly as aaee7652 prescribed — currency-blind B1 (--no-status) and memory-only recall — on a graph that actually contains supersession chains (the temporal bootstrap), and the structured edge appeared decisively (push: 0% vs 100% current across all models). The central conclusion of aaee7652 is therefore overturned: the representation edge does appear, conditional on exploitable structure + an un-confounded test." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/51338ce8-1662-4fa3-8401-9c72f8f1339b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/51338ce8-1662-4fa3-8401-9c72f8f1339b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T23:35:24.07404Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/51338ce8-1662-4fa3-8401-9c72f8f1339b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Clean currency A/B on the temporal graph: structured memory DECISIVELY beats free-text on anti-staleness (push: 0% vs 100% current, ALL models) — overturns the earlier \"structured representation never wins\" (aaee7652)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/547fdfde-6ab5-4cbd-a820-2eca7cd836ea> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/547fdfde-6ab5-4cbd-a820-2eca7cd836ea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: A session's final message is a status report, not a decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/547fdfde-6ab5-4cbd-a820-2eca7cd836ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/547fdfde-6ab5-4cbd-a820-2eca7cd836ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The predecessor lesson correctly identified auto-capture noise but prescribed a timing-scoped abstention gate. Implemented 2026-07-15, it was falsified the same day (three status-message ADs minted within hours, one captured mid-discussion of the problem). Maintainer verdict: prompt/build statuses do not belong in the graph at all — the discriminator is the channel (automatic vs deliberate), not any timing heuristic." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/547fdfde-6ab5-4cbd-a820-2eca7cd836ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/547fdfde-6ab5-4cbd-a820-2eca7cd836ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-15T16:54:22.578599Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/547fdfde-6ab5-4cbd-a820-2eca7cd836ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: A session's final message is a status report, not a decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/55085499-364f-4a78-bc06-a2df0c443ed9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/55085499-364f-4a78-bc06-a2df0c443ed9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Unproven generation baselines suppress coordinate surfaces" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/55085499-364f-4a78-bc06-a2df0c443ed9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/55085499-364f-4a78-bc06-a2df0c443ed9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Branch review proved that eventual convergence was insufficient: pairing generation B positions with generation C disk text can target the wrong entity during the window, which violates the honest-silence rule for ambiguous coordinates. Generation-proven source admission replaces that residual." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/55085499-364f-4a78-bc06-a2df0c443ed9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/55085499-364f-4a78-bc06-a2df0c443ed9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-18T01:28:24.431843Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/55085499-364f-4a78-bc06-a2df0c443ed9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Unproven generation baselines suppress coordinate surfaces" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/550c7176-c22a-4814-b746-b3306c000b1a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/550c7176-c22a-4814-b746-b3306c000b1a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Python substrate: identity-boundary canonicalization of producer idiom symbols" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/550c7176-c22a-4814-b746-b3306c000b1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/550c7176-c22a-4814-b746-b3306c000b1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Review found that ingest-only canonicalization left an alias gap at the API boundary: a caller presenting scip-python's raw `pkg/__init__:` module symbol (get_entity_dossier by symbol, link_code, proposal matching) funnels through symbols::normalize_symbol / Substrate::definition_for_symbol, which only elided package versions — so the producer's actual raw module symbol could not resolve, and a hypothetical pre-existing raw-marker entity would have been orphaned while a canonical duplicate was minted. The replacement moves canonicalization to the shared identity boundary: one scheme-dispatched lang::canonical_symbol backs both scip ingest and normalize_symbol, so stored identities and caller-provided symbols can never drift. Migration was verified unnecessary: SPARQL over the project store shows zero CodeEntity with a scip-python or __init__ substrate symbol, and the feature has never shipped." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/550c7176-c22a-4814-b746-b3306c000b1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/550c7176-c22a-4814-b746-b3306c000b1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-18T23:55:47.743839Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/550c7176-c22a-4814-b746-b3306c000b1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Python substrate: identity-boundary canonicalization of producer idiom symbols" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/558acbcf-5aae-4bfa-9d91-10e2e68ea367> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/558acbcf-5aae-4bfa-9d91-10e2e68ea367> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Retract duplicate don't-index-instance-data lesson (walk planning)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/558acbcf-5aae-4bfa-9d91-10e2e68ea367> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/558acbcf-5aae-4bfa-9d91-10e2e68ea367> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Duplicate of Lesson/89dc91bd (don't index instance data — walk planning), already covered by that Lesson plus two Constraints. Recorded during the M4 bootstrap dry-run without a list-all recall first." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/558acbcf-5aae-4bfa-9d91-10e2e68ea367> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/558acbcf-5aae-4bfa-9d91-10e2e68ea367> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-18T06:08:01.783362Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/558acbcf-5aae-4bfa-9d91-10e2e68ea367> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: retract Don't index instance data — MOOSE uses walk planning for precise, auditable recall" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/588b3f17-8dfa-4290-990f-28fbc98d2ea2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/588b3f17-8dfa-4290-990f-28fbc98d2ea2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: in-place status/retract transition" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/588b3f17-8dfa-4290-990f-28fbc98d2ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/588b3f17-8dfa-4290-990f-28fbc98d2ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Half of the prior requirement is now implemented: supersede works on any InformationRecord kind (not just ArchitecturalDecision), type-preserving, in branch feat/supersede-lifecycle (commit cd80831) — verified live by retiring Constraint 0c2106ab and Requirement f1ccd65b. What remains is the OTHER half: there is still no way to transition a record's lifecycle status IN PLACE — e.g. mark a Requirement implemented/accepted, or retract/deprecate it — without replacing it via supersede. Dogfood evidence: this very requirement cannot be marked \"implemented\" without superseding it (which marks it \"superseded\", not \"done\"). Narrowing the requirement to that remaining gap." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/588b3f17-8dfa-4290-990f-28fbc98d2ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/588b3f17-8dfa-4290-990f-28fbc98d2ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-18T05:18:28.243587Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/588b3f17-8dfa-4290-990f-28fbc98d2ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Add an in-place status/retract transition for knowledge records" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/5e8e2a69-a7af-41df-a8bf-23ead1ecb62f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/5e8e2a69-a7af-41df-a8bf-23ead1ecb62f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: A-box dense only as a bounded seed" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/5e8e2a69-a7af-41df-a8bf-23ead1ecb62f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/5e8e2a69-a7af-41df-a8bf-23ead1ecb62f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "71637748 banned A-box vector indexing as a \"vector-index/RAG trap.\" The new design addresses that concern rather than ignoring it: dense is a bounded SEED that feeds symbolic walk planning (not a replacement), gated by a confidence floor that preserves honest-empty-state, with symbolic-first anchoring keeping the symbolic layer primary; and a durable+incremental index removes the startup-cost objection (warm restart re-embeds nothing). The capability now exists in MOOSE core by deliberate direction change (instance vector store + search_records_hybrid), so an outright ban no longer reflects the architecture. This narrows — not abandons — the original intent: walk planning stays the precision engine." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/5e8e2a69-a7af-41df-a8bf-23ead1ecb62f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/5e8e2a69-a7af-41df-a8bf-23ead1ecb62f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-21T07:23:17.439642Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/5e8e2a69-a7af-41df-a8bf-23ead1ecb62f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Instance (A-box) dense retrieval is permitted only as a bounded SEED for get_relevant_context; walk planning remains the precision engine" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/60e567d7-87fd-4a08-b9a6-9d8c7b4f96fd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/60e567d7-87fd-4a08-b9a6-9d8c7b4f96fd> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Trial surface moves to moosedev 0.7.0; soak gate lifted for month-2" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/60e567d7-87fd-4a08-b9a6-9d8c7b4f96fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/60e567d7-87fd-4a08-b9a6-9d8c7b4f96fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Maintainer decision 2026-07-24, immediately after the month-1 checkpoint: upgrade the installed moosedev on this system to 0.7.0, so month-2 (2026-08) live work and checkpoint run entirely in the 0.7.0 regime. The soak condition is satisfied in substance — auto-capture was demoted to the journal-only path (AD 007dce15) and has run quiet on the dogfood instance — and the gate was already de-facto crossed: moose's .mcp.json launches the repo's target/release binary via --connect autospawn, so trial daemons have been on a post-v2.2 build since at least 2026-07-23, and the month-1 checkpoint itself ran cleanly on epoch 0.7.0+721698cf0251. Formalizing beats silent drift (invariant #6)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/60e567d7-87fd-4a08-b9a6-9d8c7b4f96fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/60e567d7-87fd-4a08-b9a6-9d8c7b4f96fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-24T17:35:18.676297Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/60e567d7-87fd-4a08-b9a6-9d8c7b4f96fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Trial surface moves to moosedev 0.7.0; soak gate lifted for month-2" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/715f527c-205b-4a20-95fc-fd14c60da1f2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/715f527c-205b-4a20-95fc-fd14c60da1f2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: retract Decision point: .moosedev/kg.nq, .opencode/plugins/moosedev-push.ts, src/api/handlers/mod.rs, src…" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/715f527c-205b-4a20-95fc-fd14c60da1f2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/715f527c-205b-4a20-95fc-fd14c60da1f2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Automatic Stop-hook capture noise ratified by mistake: a \"Decision point: <file list>\" card carries no decision content (maintainer verdict 2026-07-15 — such captures are prompt/build statuses, not architectural decisions, and do not belong in the working set). Part of the cleanup that demoted automatic capture to a telemetry-only journal." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/715f527c-205b-4a20-95fc-fd14c60da1f2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/715f527c-205b-4a20-95fc-fd14c60da1f2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-15T16:51:53.115576Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/715f527c-205b-4a20-95fc-fd14c60da1f2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: retract Decision point: .moosedev/kg.nq, .opencode/plugins/moosedev-push.ts, src/api/handlers/mod.rs, src…" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74f69826-3483-451e-b02b-55d030421112> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74f69826-3483-451e-b02b-55d030421112> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: didSave-debounced reindex with unconditional qualifying-save nudge" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74f69826-3483-451e-b02b-55d030421112> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74f69826-3483-451e-b02b-55d030421112> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Live verification against the running daemon (2026-07-17) refuted the micro-guard in the superseded decision: after a rebuild published, a fast revert-save arrived before the session's 2s-tick re-base, matched the STALE base_text byte-for-byte, and was suppressed — leaving the index permanently reflecting the pre-revert tree with no future nudge coming (the scripted revert cycle deterministically failed). The guard's premise (saved == base_text ⇒ positions unshifted) only holds when base_text matches the indexed generation, which is exactly what lags during the async reload cycle. Editors already skip didSave on clean buffers, so the guard defended against a rare event while creating a real missed-reconciliation race; it was removed and every qualifying save now nudges unconditionally." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74f69826-3483-451e-b02b-55d030421112> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74f69826-3483-451e-b02b-55d030421112> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-17T15:27:32.101858Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74f69826-3483-451e-b02b-55d030421112> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: didSave-debounced reindex with unconditional qualifying-save nudge" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/79a78439-165e-4b7c-a3c1-10bd97dd6476> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/79a78439-165e-4b7c-a3c1-10bd97dd6476> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Serialized didSave reindex with detached shutdown" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/79a78439-165e-4b7c-a3c1-10bd97dd6476> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/79a78439-165e-4b7c-a3c1-10bd97dd6476> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Branch review found six coupled failures in the prior lifecycle: stale didChange pushes, mixed-generation coordinates from mutable disk rebases, cross-repository and same-repository rebuild loss from pgrep/skip logic, a shutdown transition race that could join a long producer, failed-generation memoization against the wrong resampled manifest, and a crash-durability gap from missing directory fsync. Waiting per-project serialization preserves every requested reconciliation, detached shutdown bounds daemon exit, and generation-exact loading/publication keeps the editor and substrate state auditable." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/79a78439-165e-4b7c-a3c1-10bd97dd6476> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/79a78439-165e-4b7c-a3c1-10bd97dd6476> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-18T01:27:25.845971Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/79a78439-165e-4b7c-a3c1-10bd97dd6476> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Serialized didSave reindex with detached shutdown" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7a911f2e-d44b-4ec3-92b6-6ee696119fac> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7a911f2e-d44b-4ec3-92b6-6ee696119fac> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: push delivery value unproven for local models" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7a911f2e-d44b-4ec3-92b6-6ee696119fac> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7a911f2e-d44b-4ec3-92b6-6ee696119fac> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The original push AD justified itself with \"oracle (harness-injected context) scored 1.0 where pull scored 0.4 on the same weakest model.\" That is FALSE: the cache-gap 1.0 runs were FRONTIER (gpt-5.5, openai provider, confirmed in saved event logs), not a local model. No local model (gemma-26b, A3B-35b MoE, 27b-dense+thinking) clears cache-gap at any delivery — all 0.4 (see Lesson 5a0e66fe, the execution ceiling). So the cited evidence that push delivers value to weak models was a misattribution and must be withdrawn." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7a911f2e-d44b-4ec3-92b6-6ee696119fac> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7a911f2e-d44b-4ec3-92b6-6ee696119fac> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T05:00:12.319849Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7a911f2e-d44b-4ec3-92b6-6ee696119fac> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Push delivery (opencode plugin) is built and MECHANICALLY validated; its VALUE for local models is unproven — execution ceiling on code tasks, pending on recall tasks" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7bc926b9-a904-4534-b298-438a704e7e57> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7bc926b9-a904-4534-b298-438a704e7e57> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: A-box dense as a bounded seed" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7bc926b9-a904-4534-b298-438a704e7e57> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7bc926b9-a904-4534-b298-438a704e7e57> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The original lesson recorded a blanket \"don't index instance data / never vector-search get_relevant_context\" rule. That rule is narrowed by a deliberate direction change: MOOSE core now ships a coherent instance vector store with a matched embedding pair and a confidence floor, and Constraint af5ebd6d sanctions dense as a bounded seed. The lesson's enduring kernel — don't let dense replace auditable walk-planning precision — is preserved; the over-broad prohibition is corrected." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7bc926b9-a904-4534-b298-438a704e7e57> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7bc926b9-a904-4534-b298-438a704e7e57> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-21T07:26:07.134711Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/7bc926b9-a904-4534-b298-438a704e7e57> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: A-box dense retrieval is fine as a bounded SEED — the trap is dense REPLACING walk planning, not dense seeding it" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/8423e995-ce75-41c8-889c-2fb550708ea2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/8423e995-ce75-41c8-889c-2fb550708ea2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Retract duplicate shared-backend decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/8423e995-ce75-41c8-889c-2fb550708ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/8423e995-ce75-41c8-889c-2fb550708ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Duplicate of ArchitecturalDecision/0d81e237 (the canonical, more detailed M5 shared-backend decision). Recorded during the M4 bootstrap dry-run without a list-all recall first." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/8423e995-ce75-41c8-889c-2fb550708ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/8423e995-ce75-41c8-889c-2fb550708ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-18T06:08:01.782556Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/8423e995-ce75-41c8-889c-2fb550708ea2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: retract Shared --serve backend with thin --connect proxies for concurrent multi-client access" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/8f42538f-3c46-4e03-be7d-c700d1ccd2b1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/8f42538f-3c46-4e03-be7d-c700d1ccd2b1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: UUID deep links dispatch to canonical typed record interfaces" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/8f42538f-3c46-4e03-be7d-c700d1ccd2b1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/8f42538f-3c46-4e03-be7d-c700d1ccd2b1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The generic RecordPage made the same ADR, Requirement, or Lesson look different depending on whether it was reached from an external UUID link or selected in its UI list. The corrected contract routes typed records into their established generated-artifact interfaces while retaining the generic fallback required for Constraints and unsupported kinds." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/8f42538f-3c46-4e03-be7d-c700d1ccd2b1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/8f42538f-3c46-4e03-be7d-c700d1ccd2b1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-10T05:20:33.097334Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/8f42538f-3c46-4e03-be7d-c700d1ccd2b1> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: UUID deep links dispatch to canonical typed record interfaces" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/94851bc0-5787-45fc-98b1-61c3a8111a44> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/94851bc0-5787-45fc-98b1-61c3a8111a44> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: De-saturation lifts hybrid end-to-end answering" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/94851bc0-5787-45fc-98b1-61c3a8111a44> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "mcp" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/94851bc0-5787-45fc-98b1-61c3a8111a44> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The tooluse figures (12/24 vs 14/24) were a grading artifact, not a model weakness. The 120k escape threshold (calibrated for single-push ORACLE ~50k) mis-flags legitimate 3-4 tool-call cells, which reach 120-190k via codex's cumulative per-turn prompt accounting, not source-reading: all 10 cells in 120-250k made >=3 MCP calls AND scored 1.0 (successes counted as misses). Re-grading escape at >250k corrects it." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/94851bc0-5787-45fc-98b1-61c3a8111a44> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/94851bc0-5787-45fc-98b1-61c3a8111a44> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-21T20:19:05.735664Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/94851bc0-5787-45fc-98b1-61c3a8111a44> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: De-saturation lifts hybrid end-to-end answering" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/952b72d1-a480-40b8-9fc0-6d5483fe3a2c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/952b72d1-a480-40b8-9fc0-6d5483fe3a2c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cross-corpus currency: structured guarantees current, free-text gambles" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/952b72d1-a480-40b8-9fc0-6d5483fe3a2c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/952b72d1-a480-40b8-9fc0-6d5483fe3a2c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Across both temporally-bootstrapped corpora — moosedev-temporal (4 pairs) + burrow-temporal (3 pairs), N>=5/cell, codex gpt-5.4-mini + gpt-5.3-codex-spark, oracle+tooluse, graded by coverage-of-current-markers (Lesson 9fc21dc0): (1) B2 get_relevant_context NEVER SERVED a superseded record on any of the 7 pairs — current-only by construction (verified in pre-flight + 0 stale-served across all runs). The single B2 non-current answer (burrow report_voice, tooluse, 1/21) was the agent IGNORING memory and confabulating from the harness AGENTS.md/opencode.json overlay ('this project's local files don't define a synthesis-system rule') — a tooluse pull-gap, NOT the retrieval mechanism failing. (2) B1-rag currency-blind BM25 served current on 6/7 pairs (wherever the current record ranks >= the superseded) and collapsed only on the 1 RANK-INVERTED pair (moosedev glrc: 46% overall, ~8% in oracle/push) where the superseded record outranks the current in BM25. (3) burrow added 3 pairs, ALL non-rank-inverted -> 3 ties (quickstart, rest_rss, report_voice all ~100%/100%); rank-inversion thus occurred 1/7 (~14%) across organic histories — partly because the temporal-capture skill writes self-announcing current records (they narrate the reversal, so they carry both old+new keywords and rank well in BM25). (4) REGIME: the catastrophe is worst in oracle/push (stale top hit injected) and recovers in tooluse (agent digs past it); burrow's ties hold in both modes. NET CLAIM: structured currency is INSURANCE — an absolute guarantee (rank/corpus/model/regime-independent) against a free-text failure mode that is RARE but CATASTROPHIC (a confident, wrong, stale answer); it is NOT a uniform currency-accuracy win, since free-text ties whenever the current record ranks well (the common case). Honest scoping: demonstrating the structured ADVANTAGE requires a rank-inverted pair, which is uncommon organically, so the defensible value is the GUARANTEE, not an average-case delta. Generalizes/refines the moosedev-only currency results (Rationale abe11031, 2e88601d) to N=2 corpora; uses the burrow temporal bootstrap (Lesson 2d79b2d2) and tasks_public/burrow-temporal/*_currency.json." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/952b72d1-a480-40b8-9fc0-6d5483fe3a2c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "proposed" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/952b72d1-a480-40b8-9fc0-6d5483fe3a2c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-20T06:55:47.634627Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/952b72d1-a480-40b8-9fc0-6d5483fe3a2c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Cross-corpus currency conclusion (moosedev + burrow, 7 reversal pairs, N=2 corpora): structured = absolute current-only GUARANTEE; free-text = rank-dependent gamble that ties on 6/7 and collapses only on the 1 rank-inverted pair" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/960885ad-ca1a-40ef-b4a8-a165b277b862> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/960885ad-ca1a-40ef-b4a8-a165b277b862> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: De-saturation lifts hybrid end-to-end answering" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/960885ad-ca1a-40ef-b4a8-a165b277b862> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "mcp" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/960885ad-ca1a-40ef-b4a8-a165b277b862> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record's tooluse figures (BM25F 21/24 vs hybrid 22/24) came from a score==1.0 hand-proxy, not the grader's strict-currency metric. The fixed mode-aware grader (hybrid_ab_report.py, escape 120k oracle / 250k tooluse) gives the authoritative mem-answered: tooluse BM25F 14/24 vs hybrid 19/24 — hybrid is FURTHER ahead than the proxy showed, because the old 120k cutoff over-penalized hybrid's legitimate multi-call cells (masking the edge / even inverting it to a spurious 12-vs-14 bm25f lead). Lesson: read the grader, not a proxy." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/960885ad-ca1a-40ef-b4a8-a165b277b862> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/960885ad-ca1a-40ef-b4a8-a165b277b862> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-21T20:25:57.047862Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/960885ad-ca1a-40ef-b4a8-a165b277b862> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: De-saturation lifts hybrid end-to-end answering" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a0631a99-8f7a-453d-ba03-60ad78c48d42> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a0631a99-8f7a-453d-ba03-60ad78c48d42> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Instrument B (regraded): hybrid = -19% tokens + objprop/oracle edge; tooluse is a tie" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a0631a99-8f7a-453d-ba03-60ad78c48d42> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a0631a99-8f7a-453d-ba03-60ad78c48d42> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The free regrade (after fixing the two hybrid_ab_report.py grading bugs) OVERTURNED the prior 'drift/tooluse +20pp' headline I recorded in 75f622d7. That gap was an ARTIFACT: the stale-flag + materialize_tree-blind escape proxy over-penalized BM25F's correct-but-narrating / high-token tooluse cells (BM25F tooluse 10/20 -> 18/20 after the fix). Corrected, tooluse is a near-tie (hybrid 19/20 vs bm25f 18/20); hybrid's real edge is in oracle/objprop coverage (5/5 vs 2/5) plus the -19% token efficiency. Recording the regraded result so the live finding is honest rather than the inflated one." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a0631a99-8f7a-453d-ba03-60ad78c48d42> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a0631a99-8f7a-453d-ba03-60ad78c48d42> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-22T20:50:45.724465Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a0631a99-8f7a-453d-ba03-60ad78c48d42> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Instrument B (regraded): hybrid = -19% tokens + objprop/oracle edge; tooluse is a tie" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a08fb20f-0e0c-4775-bca6-e5315a479fdf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a08fb20f-0e0c-4775-bca6-e5315a479fdf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: local no-pull confounded by tool presentation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a08fb20f-0e0c-4775-bca6-e5315a479fdf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a08fb20f-0e0c-4775-bca6-e5315a479fdf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The original lesson concluded local-no-pull is \"a model property, not an opencode artifact.\" That is overstated. (1) Pull was measured WITHOUT controlling tool presentation — the full ~9-tool moosedev surface, passive tool descriptions, amid all of opencode's own tools — a known-bad setup for small-model tool selection; so the \"model property\" claim is not established until retested with a recall-only single tool + a directive description + a single-param schema. (2) On execution-heavy tasks (cache-gap) the pull question is moot anyway, because local models cannot act on the lesson even when it is handed to them in-prompt (oracle=0.4 — Lesson 5a0e66fe)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a08fb20f-0e0c-4775-bca6-e5315a479fdf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a08fb20f-0e0c-4775-bca6-e5315a479fdf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T05:00:32.795405Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a08fb20f-0e0c-4775-bca6-e5315a479fdf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Local models did not PULL memory as-tested — but tool presentation was an untested confound, and on execution-heavy tasks pull is moot (execution ceiling)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a40b9f68-3627-4a5f-9860-2ba8cef084e7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a40b9f68-3627-4a5f-9860-2ba8cef084e7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: recall precision via walk, no A-box index" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a40b9f68-3627-4a5f-9860-2ba8cef084e7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a40b9f68-3627-4a5f-9860-2ba8cef084e7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Correction: MOOSE was deliberately designed NOT to build a semantic/vector index over instance (A-box) data — walk planning exists precisely to avoid that imprecise-RAG trap and deliver more precise, auditable results. The superseded requirement proposed embedding-ranked A-box recall and embedding-based instance reconciliation, which reintroduces exactly that trap (violates invariants #1 symbolic-primary and #8 leverage-MOOSE). The precise retrieval path already exists symbolically, so the real work is tool selection, not a new index." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a40b9f68-3627-4a5f-9860-2ba8cef084e7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a40b9f68-3627-4a5f-9860-2ba8cef084e7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-18T04:57:08.718081Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a40b9f68-3627-4a5f-9860-2ba8cef084e7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Improve recall precision via symbolic walk/sparql + tool-selection guidance (no A-box vector index)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a621fda7-61ce-4b92-bf08-47a143d558fe> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a621fda7-61ce-4b92-bf08-47a143d558fe> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: One verification pass: subagents don't run the full test suite" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a621fda7-61ce-4b92-bf08-47a143d558fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a621fda7-61ce-4b92-bf08-47a143d558fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Text-only correction: the original record's description contained a stray garbled character (\"and每 toggling\") introduced at capture time. Content and claim are unchanged; superseding rather than silently editing, per the correction discipline." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a621fda7-61ce-4b92-bf08-47a143d558fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a621fda7-61ce-4b92-bf08-47a143d558fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-07T03:29:49.442449Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a621fda7-61ce-4b92-bf08-47a143d558fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: One verification pass: subagents don't run the full test suite" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ab1777b1-b810-46da-89d4-3a22d05d2563> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ab1777b1-b810-46da-89d4-3a22d05d2563> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Capability Stage-1 (N=3): categorical win across all four classes" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ab1777b1-b810-46da-89d4-3a22d05d2563> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ab1777b1-b810-46da-89d4-3a22d05d2563> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Tightened N=3 re-run with the 15-question suite (n=7-11/cell) refines the N=1 numbers and adds the honest threshold + multi-hop precision-artifact analysis; supersedes the N=1 finding as the current capability result." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ab1777b1-b810-46da-89d4-3a22d05d2563> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ab1777b1-b810-46da-89d4-3a22d05d2563> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-23T02:58:35.484633Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ab1777b1-b810-46da-89d4-3a22d05d2563> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Capability Stage-1 (N=3): categorical win across all four classes" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/abe11031-8ec9-4ac4-bf3e-49bbb5884e87> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/abe11031-8ec9-4ac4-bf3e-49bbb5884e87> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: 4 reversal pairs, structured guarantees current" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/abe11031-8ec9-4ac4-bf3e-49bbb5884e87> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/abe11031-8ec9-4ac4-bf3e-49bbb5884e87> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Tested 3 additional reversal pairs to check whether the get_relevant_context currency win generalizes. It does NOT generalize as a universal free-text failure: B2 guarantees current on all 4 pairs, but B1 failed catastrophically only on get_relevant_context (where the superseded record outranks the current in BM25) and recovered on the other 3 (where the current record ranks well and self-announces). So the accurate claim is structured GUARANTEE vs free-text content/rank-dependent gamble, not a flat 0%-vs-100% — a scope correction to the single-pair result." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/abe11031-8ec9-4ac4-bf3e-49bbb5884e87> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/abe11031-8ec9-4ac4-bf3e-49bbb5884e87> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T23:50:30.250542Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/abe11031-8ec9-4ac4-bf3e-49bbb5884e87> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Currency A/B across 4 reversal pairs: structured memory GUARANTEES current (B2 100%/pair, all models); free-text currency is a RANK-dependent gamble — catastrophic (0%) only when the superseded record outranks the current in BM25, else it recovers (~100%)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/af982cc8-7304-4937-b4e6-026c23f402ce> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/af982cc8-7304-4937-b4e6-026c23f402ce> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: align_concepts: defn_cosine is discarded; sharpening class definitions made it worse" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/af982cc8-7304-4937-b4e6-026c23f402ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/af982cc8-7304-4937-b4e6-026c23f402ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded version reported \"7/12 positives (58%, up from 8%)\" without discounting contaminated probe cases, and predated the measured failure of the ontology-definition curation pass. Both the headline number and the recommended next step were wrong; the mechanism diagnosis was not." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/af982cc8-7304-4937-b4e6-026c23f402ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/af982cc8-7304-4937-b4e6-026c23f402ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-29T20:55:44.639944Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/af982cc8-7304-4937-b4e6-026c23f402ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: align_concepts: defn_cosine is discarded; sharpening class definitions made it worse" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b696b181-9469-498c-9649-70e62a517d6a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b696b181-9469-498c-9649-70e62a517d6a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Editor hardening with live-clearable workbench links and serialized clients" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b696b181-9469-498c-9649-70e62a517d6a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b696b181-9469-498c-9649-70e62a517d6a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record encoded two false lifecycle subclaims. OnceLock could not withdraw an in-process workbench address when Axum stopped, and saying http.addr existed solely for --status/ui omitted the Claude and OpenCode HTTP adapters. Its first VS Code repair also left clients invisible until start() completed, so stopAll and deactivation could miss them and failed asynchronous disposal went unobserved. Clearable publication plus serialized, visible client lifecycle replaces those gaps while preserving the thin-client architecture." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b696b181-9469-498c-9649-70e62a517d6a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b696b181-9469-498c-9649-70e62a517d6a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-19T16:27:51.476065Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b696b181-9469-498c-9649-70e62a517d6a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Editor hardening with live-clearable workbench links and serialized clients" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ba36f709-f264-4d3d-9a26-13e1a3fc46cb> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ba36f709-f264-4d3d-9a26-13e1a3fc46cb> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: http.addr is identity-verified across every HTTP consumer" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ba36f709-f264-4d3d-9a26-13e1a3fc46cb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ba36f709-f264-4d3d-9a26-13e1a3fc46cb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record overclaimed completeness: it omitted the OpenCode checkpoint adapter, accepted non-successful or redirected JSON in the Rust verifier, and withdrew only the disk file when Axum ended while leaving the in-process OnceLock permanently set. The replacement applies one explicit direct-success identity contract to every HTTP consumer and makes both disk and in-process publications follow server lifetime." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ba36f709-f264-4d3d-9a26-13e1a3fc46cb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ba36f709-f264-4d3d-9a26-13e1a3fc46cb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-19T16:28:14.80828Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ba36f709-f264-4d3d-9a26-13e1a3fc46cb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: http.addr is identity-verified across every HTTP consumer" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbe1c15a-7ad3-40a2-875b-a0c9c295f62b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbe1c15a-7ad3-40a2-875b-a0c9c295f62b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: retract Decision point: .claude/hooks/moosedev-push.sh, .moosedev/kg.nq, ontologies/software-code.ttl, on…" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbe1c15a-7ad3-40a2-875b-a0c9c295f62b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbe1c15a-7ad3-40a2-875b-a0c9c295f62b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Mechanical automatic capture recorded a file-list checkpoint after the session's deliberate typed knowledge was already captured. It is redundant inbox noise, not an architectural decision." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbe1c15a-7ad3-40a2-875b-a0c9c295f62b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbe1c15a-7ad3-40a2-875b-a0c9c295f62b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-15T00:41:10.92689Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbe1c15a-7ad3-40a2-875b-a0c9c295f62b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: retract Decision point: .claude/hooks/moosedev-push.sh, .moosedev/kg.nq, ontologies/software-code.ttl, on…" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bcfefed1-e3c3-4030-80d6-cd70a1d3a2fe> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bcfefed1-e3c3-4030-80d6-cd70a1d3a2fe> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Recall replies budget by priority: prose first, links last, nothing dropped early" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bcfefed1-e3c3-4030-80d6-cd70a1d3a2fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bcfefed1-e3c3-4030-80d6-cd70a1d3a2fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record described the second pass as spending the remaining budget \"in original order\", and that stopped being true: order is now an explicit priority, because two successive review findings showed order is the only thing that can keep the prose guarantee. Grouping prose ahead of links still let an oversized literal defer alongside a description and take the second pass first; and a per-value floor means ~166 distinct properties exhaust the budget on their own, which no division of the remainder fixes. It also predates identity fields being clipped against the record's share and the fair share becoming a gate rather than a clip. Leaving it would misdescribe how the tool actually shortens." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bcfefed1-e3c3-4030-80d6-cd70a1d3a2fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bcfefed1-e3c3-4030-80d6-cd70a1d3a2fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-07T16:16:54.118644Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bcfefed1-e3c3-4030-80d6-cd70a1d3a2fe> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Recall replies budget by priority: prose first, links last, nothing dropped early" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bd2042a1-3e4e-4f9e-8173-b503f0f35d4e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bd2042a1-3e4e-4f9e-8173-b503f0f35d4e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: flat graph, capture gap not ontology" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bd2042a1-3e4e-4f9e-8173-b503f0f35d4e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bd2042a1-3e4e-4f9e-8173-b503f0f35d4e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The prior finding (f36482eb) established that the capture surface creates no inter-record edges except supersession, but did not localize the gap to a layer. A follow-up sparql over the loaded ontology's owl:ObjectProperty definitions shows the architecture ontology DOES define the needed relationship vocabulary, so the model is adequate and the gap is specifically the MCP WRITE PATH — not the ontology. This re-points the fix at the tooling layer." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bd2042a1-3e4e-4f9e-8173-b503f0f35d4e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bd2042a1-3e4e-4f9e-8173-b503f0f35d4e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T07:00:26.354224Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bd2042a1-3e4e-4f9e-8173-b503f0f35d4e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: The flat graph is a CAPTURE/TOOLING gap, NOT an ontology gap: the architecture ontology defines a rich relationship vocabulary (violates, concerns, constrains, isMotivatedBy, learnedFrom, resultsIn, weighs, supersedes) but the MCP write tools populate only supersedes + hasRationale" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c010367f-f0b8-4bb2-a69c-b74ab279fcfd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c010367f-f0b8-4bb2-a69c-b74ab279fcfd> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Typed artifacts share UUID routes and one-hop relationship graphs" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c010367f-f0b8-4bb2-a69c-b74ab279fcfd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex-mcp-client" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c010367f-f0b8-4bb2-a69c-b74ab279fcfd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Constraints now need the same first-class interface and canonical UUID routing as ADRs, Requirements, and Lessons, so the previous decision's Constraint generic fallback is obsolete. Full generated-artifact parity was chosen over a UI-only Constraint list to preserve the shared artifact contract. A fixed graph above content was chosen over tabs or a split view so relationships and record text remain visible in one reading flow. Reusing the generic record-detail endpoint was chosen over adding per-artifact neighborhood fields or a second graph endpoint, keeping one relationship query policy." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c010367f-f0b8-4bb2-a69c-b74ab279fcfd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c010367f-f0b8-4bb2-a69c-b74ab279fcfd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-10T06:23:45.631307Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c010367f-f0b8-4bb2-a69c-b74ab279fcfd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Typed artifacts share UUID routes and one-hop relationship graphs" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c0e7af2f-54a9-44a1-b5d1-81c37bb51341> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c0e7af2f-54a9-44a1-b5d1-81c37bb51341> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Recall replies are budget-bounded, truncating rather than dropping" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c0e7af2f-54a9-44a1-b5d1-81c37bb51341> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c0e7af2f-54a9-44a1-b5d1-81c37bb51341> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record claimed values are \"clipped on char boundaries\" to leave a relevance lead, but that path was unreachable as written: the value was clipped to the whole remaining room and the marker, key, and newline were added afterwards, so every truncated line exceeded the budget and was dropped instead. Long descriptions vanished entirely rather than leaving a lead. The record even cited \"0 value(s) truncated\" from live measurement as evidence the design worked, when it was evidence truncation never fired. Also corrects the bound: labels are `rdfs:label` and unbounded on imported records, so charging them to a record's share without clipping them left the declared ceiling untrue. Both found by a code review, 2026-08-06, and now regression-locked." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c0e7af2f-54a9-44a1-b5d1-81c37bb51341> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c0e7af2f-54a9-44a1-b5d1-81c37bb51341> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-06T23:51:44.469001Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c0e7af2f-54a9-44a1-b5d1-81c37bb51341> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Recall replies are budget-bounded, truncating rather than dropping" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c490a03d-6f26-4679-9075-c8668af1426c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c490a03d-6f26-4679-9075-c8668af1426c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: no execution ceiling, injection enabled fix" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c490a03d-6f26-4679-9075-c8668af1426c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c490a03d-6f26-4679-9075-c8668af1426c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Last session's \"execution ceiling\" rested on two errors, both refuted by primary evidence. (a) B0+oracle injects no context: run.py:176 gates injection on `mode=='oracle' AND arm!='B0'`, so the dense-27b/gemma/A3B \"oracle 0.4\" runs cited as the ceiling (18665903, 41dbc597, ea9687d9) were actually COLD runs — a category error. (b) The genuine local push success (e0ee0429, B2-oracle, A3B, score 1.0) was misread as frontier by generalizing from a DIFFERENT 1.0 run (884fe011, which is frontier-cold B0-tooluse) instead of checking e0ee0429's own identity; agent_model=lmstudio/qwen3.6-35b-a3b-mlx + a 1.697M-token local fingerprint (frontier runs here are ≤177k) + a complete cross-module patch confirm it was the local A3B. Net: memory injection took a local model 0.4→1.0 on the multi-module cache-gap task; no ceiling exists." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c490a03d-6f26-4679-9075-c8668af1426c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c490a03d-6f26-4679-9075-c8668af1426c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T05:24:06.250137Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c490a03d-6f26-4679-9075-c8668af1426c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: No execution ceiling — a local model made the FULL multi-module cache-gap fix when the record was INJECTED (push/B2-oracle = 1.0) vs 0.4 cold/pull; the earlier \"ceiling\" was a B0-oracle artifact plus a provider misread" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c7c843cd-d762-45a6-982e-adf860a309ab> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c7c843cd-d762-45a6-982e-adf860a309ab> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Month-1 checkpoint: trivyn gap widened; moose null under re-architecture churn" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c7c843cd-d762-45a6-982e-adf860a309ab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c7c843cd-d762-45a6-982e-adf860a309ab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Maintainer supplied the missing context for the moose null: moose underwent heavy re-architecting in the two weeks before the checkpoint, which the original record attributed generically to \"locally recoverable rationale or noise\". Git evidence confirms ~20× trivyn's churn, so the null gets a specific mechanism and a pre-registered forward prediction instead of a vague caveat." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c7c843cd-d762-45a6-982e-adf860a309ab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c7c843cd-d762-45a6-982e-adf860a309ab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-24T16:59:18.997987Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/c7c843cd-d762-45a6-982e-adf860a309ab> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Month-1 checkpoint: trivyn gap widened; moose null under re-architecture churn" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ccfac08f-0221-4a0b-b690-2dedc02be062> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ccfac08f-0221-4a0b-b690-2dedc02be062> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: push/injection delivery is built and evidence-supported" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ccfac08f-0221-4a0b-b690-2dedc02be062> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ccfac08f-0221-4a0b-b690-2dedc02be062> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The prior AD downgraded push to \"value unproven — execution ceiling.\" That downgrade rested on the now-refuted ceiling claim (see the Lesson superseding 5a0e66fe). Primary evidence — run.py:176 oracle-arm gating (B0+oracle = cold), the e0ee0429 patch (full cross-module implementation), and agent_model + the 1.697M-token local fingerprint — shows the only genuine injection test on a local model scored 1.0 and was the only condition to beat 0.4. Push value for local models is therefore supported (n=1, pending replication), not unproven." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ccfac08f-0221-4a0b-b690-2dedc02be062> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ccfac08f-0221-4a0b-b690-2dedc02be062> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T05:24:22.905811Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ccfac08f-0221-4a0b-b690-2dedc02be062> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Push/injection delivery: built, mechanically validated, AND evidence-supported — injecting the record took a local model 0.4→1.0 on the multi-module cache-gap task (the only condition that worked)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d1354c56-592a-40ef-aaab-ab53f125d8d5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d1354c56-592a-40ef-aaab-ab53f125d8d5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Generation-proven session-pinned LSP coordinates" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d1354c56-592a-40ef-aaab-ab53f125d8d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d1354c56-592a-40ef-aaab-ab53f125d8d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Branch review found six correctness gaps in the earlier decision: didChange could leave stale pushed diagnostics; mutable disk text could be paired with a different immutable substrate generation; global pgrep/skip behavior could discard another repository's or a newer same-repository rebuild; shutdown could race into joining a long index; an internal manifest retry could memoize the wrong failed identity; and missing parent-directory fsync weakened crash durability. The replacement uses deterministic generation evidence, explicit refresh boundaries, per-project serialization, and non-joining shutdown so ambiguous coordinates and uncertain lifecycle state degrade honestly instead of being guessed or dropped." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d1354c56-592a-40ef-aaab-ab53f125d8d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d1354c56-592a-40ef-aaab-ab53f125d8d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-18T01:27:08.232791Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/d1354c56-592a-40ef-aaab-ab53f125d8d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Generation-proven session-pinned LSP coordinates" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/da3ca7e3-f960-4823-88e8-81b6f5d65771> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/da3ca7e3-f960-4823-88e8-81b6f5d65771> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Per-project index lock serializes every producer" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/da3ca7e3-f960-4823-88e8-81b6f5d65771> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/da3ca7e3-f960-4823-88e8-81b6f5d65771> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The earlier lesson's pgrep-and-manual-wait workaround and open fix direction are obsolete. The implemented per-project waiting lock now serializes all writers, while branch review showed that pgrep and if-idle skipping could lose both cross-repository and same-repository reconciliation." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/da3ca7e3-f960-4823-88e8-81b6f5d65771> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/da3ca7e3-f960-4823-88e8-81b6f5d65771> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-18T01:28:35.246116Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/da3ca7e3-f960-4823-88e8-81b6f5d65771> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Per-project index lock serializes every producer" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/dbae9fe2-a423-4cd0-9367-1e9595613cfd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/dbae9fe2-a423-4cd0-9367-1e9595613cfd> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Mint-gap visibility is the LAST dossier rung, below substrate coverage" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/dbae9fe2-a423-4cd0-9367-1e9595613cfd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/dbae9fe2-a423-4cd0-9367-1e9595613cfd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded record described the unminted rung as checked BEFORE the position-specific substrate rungs, and that ordering shipped as a defect. It made a never-indexed project answer \"run mint\" instead of \"run index\" (caught by tests/mcp_replies.rs::dossier_position_reports_unavailable_substrate), and it masked the coverage report for files outside the substrate — destroying the three-way discrimination AD a8f95059 exists to provide, and handing users advice that could not help them. Corrected by a code review, 2026-08-06." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/dbae9fe2-a423-4cd0-9367-1e9595613cfd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/dbae9fe2-a423-4cd0-9367-1e9595613cfd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-06T23:51:16.818621Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/dbae9fe2-a423-4cd0-9367-1e9595613cfd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Mint-gap visibility is the LAST dossier rung, below substrate coverage" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/deadcb05-97ad-403e-817c-dd47cfbb92d3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/deadcb05-97ad-403e-817c-dd47cfbb92d3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: retract With a module-level link in place, token-less positions (comments, blank lines) surface the module dossier via rust-analyzer whole-file module occurrences - 2026-07-08 acceptance finding, resolution pending" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/deadcb05-97ad-403e-817c-dd47cfbb92d3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "phase7-acceptance" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/deadcb05-97ad-403e-817c-dd47cfbb92d3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Resolved: AD ab379ef4 (whole-file module occurrences are not position hits) removed the module fallback - token-less positions now miss honestly, so this consequence no longer holds." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/deadcb05-97ad-403e-817c-dd47cfbb92d3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/deadcb05-97ad-403e-817c-dd47cfbb92d3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-09T14:41:49.542636Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/deadcb05-97ad-403e-817c-dd47cfbb92d3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: retract With a module-level link in place, token-less positions (comments, blank lines) surface the module dossier via rust-analyzer whole-file module occurrences - 2026-07-08 acceptance finding, resolution pending" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e07a009a-9023-4688-95e6-123a1104913a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e07a009a-9023-4688-95e6-123a1104913a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Automatic capture is a telemetry journal, not a record minter" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e07a009a-9023-4688-95e6-123a1104913a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e07a009a-9023-4688-95e6-123a1104913a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded design kept minting proposed ADs and relied on a since-last-stamp abstention window plus inbox triage to absorb noise. Same-day evidence falsified it: sessions that wrote no typed records in the window still minted pure status chatter (three specimens within hours, one captured mid-discussion of this very problem), and the empirical ratification rate of ALL automatic captures ever is zero. The right symbolic boundary is the channel itself — automatic ⇒ journal, deliberate ⇒ record — not a timing heuristic over content the system cannot judge." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e07a009a-9023-4688-95e6-123a1104913a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e07a009a-9023-4688-95e6-123a1104913a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-15T16:52:15.837306Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e07a009a-9023-4688-95e6-123a1104913a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Automatic capture is a telemetry journal, not a record minter" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ea048a36-f38d-416c-9732-4ba98f33e5c0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ea048a36-f38d-416c-9732-4ba98f33e5c0> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: retract Decision point: .claude/hooks/moosedev-push.sh, .moosedev/kg.nq, ontologies/software-code.ttl, on…" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ea048a36-f38d-416c-9732-4ba98f33e5c0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ea048a36-f38d-416c-9732-4ba98f33e5c0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Mechanical automatic capture recorded a file-list checkpoint after the session's deliberate typed knowledge was already captured. It is redundant inbox noise, not an architectural decision." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ea048a36-f38d-416c-9732-4ba98f33e5c0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ea048a36-f38d-416c-9732-4ba98f33e5c0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-15T00:41:09.615523Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ea048a36-f38d-416c-9732-4ba98f33e5c0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: retract Decision point: .claude/hooks/moosedev-push.sh, .moosedev/kg.nq, ontologies/software-code.ttl, on…" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee150eab-c520-48b2-849e-2621fbecd1b7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee150eab-c520-48b2-849e-2621fbecd1b7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: pull gap is real, push closes it" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee150eab-c520-48b2-849e-2621fbecd1b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee150eab-c520-48b2-849e-2621fbecd1b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded lesson claimed pull is moot on execution-heavy tasks because local models hit an execution ceiling. That premise is false (e0ee0429: A3B B2-oracle = 1.0, full multi-module patch — see the Lesson superseding 5a0e66fe). Pull-vs-push is therefore a real, live comparison on coding tasks, and the current evidence shows push closing the pull gap (0.4→1.0). The valid parts (local-no-pull as-tested; the tool-presentation confound) are retained." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee150eab-c520-48b2-849e-2621fbecd1b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee150eab-c520-48b2-849e-2621fbecd1b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T05:24:29.9739Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee150eab-c520-48b2-849e-2621fbecd1b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Pull gap is real (local models don't retrieve/act → 0.4 at B2-tooluse) and PUSH closes it (B2-oracle = 1.0); the \"pull moot via execution ceiling\" clause is withdrawn; pull's presentation-confound is still open" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee42fef4-9089-4921-8b33-9315a60f7a99> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee42fef4-9089-4921-8b33-9315a60f7a99> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Instrument B (corrected): hybrid wins drift; anti-cases were grading artifacts" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee42fef4-9089-4921-8b33-9315a60f7a99> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee42fef4-9089-4921-8b33-9315a60f7a99> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Free transcript inspection (no agent re-run) showed BOTH anti-case caveats in the superseded version were GRADING ARTIFACTS, not hybrid weaknesses. objprop_validate's low mem% is the stale-marker narration false-positive (extends Lesson 9fc21dc0): the matcher trips on backtick-wrapped negation ('no `debug_assert`') AND on the stale marker 'debug-only' which is literally in the CURRENT decision's own title ('...without debug-only panics'), so citing the canonical decision self-trips — under coverage (the 9fc21dc0-endorsed verdict) hybrid WINS objprop (full coverage 5/5 oracle vs bm25f 2/5). geospatial's 'regression' is one cell's 339k-token internal reasoning thrash tripping the tooluse escape proxy on a materialize_tree=False task with NO source to escape to (answer was correct, 224 chars, 1 tool call) — a tie, not a regression. Correcting the record so the live finding reflects the strengthened result and names the two harness bugs." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee42fef4-9089-4921-8b33-9315a60f7a99> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee42fef4-9089-4921-8b33-9315a60f7a99> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-22T20:29:09.141039Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee42fef4-9089-4921-8b33-9315a60f7a99> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Instrument B (corrected): hybrid wins drift; anti-cases were grading artifacts" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee5cbe86-48df-4fec-b078-4d16353452be> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee5cbe86-48df-4fec-b078-4d16353452be> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: GROWL enrich co-locates inferred edges in kg/project" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee5cbe86-48df-4fec-b078-4d16353452be> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/11e01ea2-f520-4f7c-a165-09532dacd43f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee5cbe86-48df-4fec-b078-4d16353452be> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee5cbe86-48df-4fec-b078-4d16353452be> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Reading Trivyn's actual enrich implementation (trivyn/src/rdf/reasoning.rs) showed materialize_property_inferences writes inferred triples INTO the data graph + per-triple RDF-star prov, NOT a separate inferred named graph (that's only Trivyn's full-reasoning path, run_reasoning). And confirmed moosedev's get_relevant_context expansion reads are all kg/project-scoped (record_neighbors src/graph/mod.rs:1585, build_context_item:1760, list_instances:1728), so co-locating inferred edges in kg/project makes them first-class with zero hot-path change, while a separate kg/inferred graph would need unioning into 5-8 reads. The separate-graph placement in the superseded record predated reading Trivyn's code and the kg/project-scoped-read finding." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee5cbe86-48df-4fec-b078-4d16353452be> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee5cbe86-48df-4fec-b078-4d16353452be> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-22T03:20:15.613005Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee5cbe86-48df-4fec-b078-4d16353452be> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: GROWL enrich co-locates inferred edges in kg/project" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f0197885-403e-4112-8c7a-8a8c5df69611> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f0197885-403e-4112-8c7a-8a8c5df69611> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Ontology vector store: regenerate on any layout change, never migrate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f0197885-403e-4112-8c7a-8a8c5df69611> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "capture-probe" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f0197885-403e-4112-8c7a-8a8c5df69611> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "MOOSE 0.8.0 changed the ontology_vectors data contract, and MOOSEDev is the writer of that table. The superseded decision gated reuse on the content fingerprint alone, which cannot detect a layout change: the store on disk stayed lexically fresh while becoming unreadable, and the resulting failure was swallowed as a warning that silently disabled L2 alignment. Recording the layout generation makes the upgrade explicit and one-shot. Choosing regeneration over a migration ladder is what keeps this from recurring as a maintenance burden on every future schema change." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f0197885-403e-4112-8c7a-8a8c5df69611> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f0197885-403e-4112-8c7a-8a8c5df69611> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-12T21:11:32.518944Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f0197885-403e-4112-8c7a-8a8c5df69611> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Ontology vector store: regenerate on any layout change, never migrate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f99703a9-9688-4e82-a195-532c7be0eddd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f99703a9-9688-4e82-a195-532c7be0eddd> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Tool-level capture-gap fix is built: inline relations + suggester + advisory" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f99703a9-9688-4e82-a195-532c7be0eddd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f99703a9-9688-4e82-a195-532c7be0eddd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The \"unbuilt\" conclusion of 3f807592 is now false. Parts (a) and (b) of its prescribed fix shipped at the open-source tool layer (AD 8353c51a): record_important_decision takes inline relations (atomic, SHACL-validated); a symbolic link-suggester + suggest_links tool surface legal candidates; validate emits a non-blocking under-linked advisory. Part (c) was already done by the bootstrap skill (AD 059b01b7). One refinement vs the diagnosis: the validate nudge is a Rust/SPARQL advisory rather than declarative sh:severity sh:Warning, because MOOSE's M3 validator has no severity handling and skips sh:class/sh:or — declarative severity is a deferred MOOSE-core change." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f99703a9-9688-4e82-a195-532c7be0eddd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f99703a9-9688-4e82-a195-532c7be0eddd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-22T07:53:53.652684Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f99703a9-9688-4e82-a195-532c7be0eddd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Tool-level capture-gap fix is built: inline relations + suggester + advisory" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fa5b6ae3-bab5-4afa-a21e-ac1f18e5467b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fa5b6ae3-bab5-4afa-a21e-ac1f18e5467b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: relate() validates endpoints against SHACL shapes" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fa5b6ae3-bab5-4afa-a21e-ac1f18e5467b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex-mcp-client" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fa5b6ae3-bab5-4afa-a21e-ac1f18e5467b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The prior relate design required both endpoints to be InformationRecords, which rejected legitimate relationships to SystemComponent and allowed some predicate/object mistakes because it did not consult declared shape constraints. User correction clarified that dcam:rangeIncludes should not drive validation; SHACL shapes are the authoritative contract for relationship ranges, and trivyn:labelProperty is a typed-property mirror hint while rdfs:label remains canonical." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fa5b6ae3-bab5-4afa-a21e-ac1f18e5467b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fa5b6ae3-bab5-4afa-a21e-ac1f18e5467b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T17:07:19.956747Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fa5b6ae3-bab5-4afa-a21e-ac1f18e5467b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: relate() validates relationship endpoints against SHACL shapes; capture keeps rdfs:label canonical and mirrors it into class-specific typed properties" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fccd0ced-ab3f-4e87-a5d7-4e02e55d3d73> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fccd0ced-ab3f-4e87-a5d7-4e02e55d3d73> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: MOOSEDev read cost is moderate + query-dependent; the 1.68M was a dead-MCP grep" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fccd0ced-ab3f-4e87-a5d7-4e02e55d3d73> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fccd0ced-ab3f-4e87-a5d7-4e02e55d3d73> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "f8f2f87c attributed B2's 1.68M set-completeness cost to 'agent query competence' (the agent allegedly choosing list_mcp_resources over SPARQL). The clean re-run with a fixed MCP (Lesson 0a890ea9) shows the 1.68M was actually the DEAD-MCP grep of the store (broken MOOSEDEV_BIN), and with a working MCP B2 returns the 122-set via sparql at ~78-167k tokens (recall 1.0). So the cause was a harness bug, not query competence — there is no 'B2 payoff conditional on agent query competence' problem; gpt-5.4-mini calls the right tool reliably when the MCP works." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fccd0ced-ab3f-4e87-a5d7-4e02e55d3d73> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fccd0ced-ab3f-4e87-a5d7-4e02e55d3d73> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-23T19:17:47.866259Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fccd0ced-ab3f-4e87-a5d7-4e02e55d3d73> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: MOOSEDev read cost is moderate + query-dependent; the 1.68M was a dead-MCP grep" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fd9d65dc-b404-4d68-9216-dfe0324a459f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fd9d65dc-b404-4d68-9216-dfe0324a459f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: LSP positions track unsaved buffers by exact line alignment" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fd9d65dc-b404-4d68-9216-dfe0324a459f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex-mcp-client" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fd9d65dc-b404-4d68-9216-dfe0324a459f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Live JSON-RPC inspection on 2026-07-16 proved the daemon emitted correct saved-file ranges while Zed displayed squiggles on wrong active-buffer lines after restart/refresh. The prior saved-state-only contract ignored didOpen/didChange text, so a correct server payload could still be wrong for the editor surface. Full text synchronization plus exact line alignment fixes the user-visible bug without fuzzy entity matching." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fd9d65dc-b404-4d68-9216-dfe0324a459f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fd9d65dc-b404-4d68-9216-dfe0324a459f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-17T02:11:57.183021Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fd9d65dc-b404-4d68-9216-dfe0324a459f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: LSP positions track unsaved buffers by exact line alignment" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fe606fb8-95f2-4bae-8085-421adc804b81> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fe606fb8-95f2-4bae-8085-421adc804b81> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: MCP metadata contract, amended: instruction and worked examples are load-bearing" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fe606fb8-95f2-4bae-8085-421adc804b81> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fe606fb8-95f2-4bae-8085-421adc804b81> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Tool-description text is a capture affordance, not product copy: removing it changed recorded-knowledge coverage by an order of magnitude even though every parameter, schema, and SHACL shape stayed identical. ee900bdb's routing-contract framing is correct and retained — it was incomplete. Its implementation optimized for terseness in the one surface that is frequently the model's sole guidance, trading away instruction for concision. This amendment adds the missing obligation rather than reverting the contract, because the routing improvements (adjacent-tool disambiguation, side-effect disclosure, the recall ladder) are independently valuable and were not the regression." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fe606fb8-95f2-4bae-8085-421adc804b81> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fe606fb8-95f2-4bae-8085-421adc804b81> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-10T04:07:11.417942Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fe606fb8-95f2-4bae-8085-421adc804b81> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: MCP metadata contract, amended: instruction and worked examples are load-bearing" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/08b807a4-d7fa-4b0a-ad84-78158a4a8088> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/08b807a4-d7fa-4b0a-ad84-78158a4a8088> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Frictionless onboarding & install for external adopters" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/08b807a4-d7fa-4b0a-ad84-78158a4a8088> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "onboarding-capture" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/08b807a4-d7fa-4b0a-ad84-78158a4a8088> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Productization goal (user framing, 2026-07-01): someone other than the author must be able to install and use MOOSEDev easily, WITHOUT source access to the closed MOOSE engine. Concretely: a one-command install channel (script + Homebrew) delivering a self-contained binary, plus one-command project setup (`moosedev init`) that wires MCP config and the version-controlled memory. This is the distribution funnel (invariant #11), un-gated by the in-anger trial. Sibling to Requirement d459cac2 (version-controllable KG — the sharing enabler); distinct from Requirement 5565038e (cross-machine merge dedup — the multi-person case, deferred/trial-gated)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/08b807a4-d7fa-4b0a-ad84-78158a4a8088> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/08b807a4-d7fa-4b0a-ad84-78158a4a8088> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-04T17:37:12.171565Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/08b807a4-d7fa-4b0a-ad84-78158a4a8088> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Frictionless onboarding & install for external adopters" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/14a4275c-d688-466e-96b5-9d4b46ea593c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/14a4275c-d688-466e-96b5-9d4b46ea593c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Recall precision via symbolic walk/sparql" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/14a4275c-d688-466e-96b5-9d4b46ea593c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/14a4275c-d688-466e-96b5-9d4b46ea593c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Recall precision comes from existing symbolic mechanisms, not instance embeddings: (a) query (NLQ) gives walk-planned, synthesized, trace-bearing answers; (b) sparql gives exact structural reads; (c) get_relevant_context stays a fast, deterministic, SHALLOW anchor/browse tool — the 0.45 relevance floor is the correct honesty fix and it must NOT be upgraded to vector search. Real work item: make tool selection reliable — sharpen the get_relevant_context / query / sparql tool descriptions (and CLAUDE.md) to encode the precision/cost ladder so agents escalate from shallow anchor-recall to walk-planned reasoning. A-box reconciliation (dedup/contradiction) stays symbolic + LLM-as-sensor per Requirement b5b101dd, not vector similarity. No custom pipeline; compose existing MOOSE (invariant #8)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/14a4275c-d688-466e-96b5-9d4b46ea593c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/14a4275c-d688-466e-96b5-9d4b46ea593c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/a40b9f68-3627-4a5f-9860-2ba8cef084e7> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/14a4275c-d688-466e-96b5-9d4b46ea593c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-18T04:57:08.718081Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/14a4275c-d688-466e-96b5-9d4b46ea593c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Improve recall precision via symbolic walk/sparql + tool-selection guidance (no A-box vector index)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/14a4275c-d688-466e-96b5-9d4b46ea593c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/f1ccd65b-f816-470b-9b59-8c4f85716bb3> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/1ae3b79a-f2c5-41ba-a221-cc79bfe9edc2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/1ae3b79a-f2c5-41ba-a221-cc79bfe9edc2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Add an in-place status/retract transition for knowledge records" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/1ae3b79a-f2c5-41ba-a221-cc79bfe9edc2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/1ae3b79a-f2c5-41ba-a221-cc79bfe9edc2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "supersede_decision now generalizes the REPLACE transition to all InformationRecord subclasses, but the lifecycle still lacks a non-replacing status transition. Needed: a set-status / retract primitive that flips an existing record's hasLifecycleStatus (e.g. proposed→accepted, accepted→implemented, *→deprecated) WITHOUT minting a replacement, preserving provenance. The status vocabulary itself is thin — there is no \"implemented\"/\"done\" value distinct from \"accepted\" — so this likely also wants an explicit completed/implemented status. Until then, an implemented Requirement can only be marked by superseding it, which conflates \"fulfilled\" with \"replaced\". Relates to b5b101dd (detect/surface/supersede contradictory entries) and the read path that already hides superseded/deprecated for all kinds." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/1ae3b79a-f2c5-41ba-a221-cc79bfe9edc2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/1ae3b79a-f2c5-41ba-a221-cc79bfe9edc2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/588b3f17-8dfa-4290-990f-28fbc98d2ea2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/1ae3b79a-f2c5-41ba-a221-cc79bfe9edc2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-18T05:18:28.243587Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/1ae3b79a-f2c5-41ba-a221-cc79bfe9edc2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Add an in-place status/retract transition for knowledge records" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/1ae3b79a-f2c5-41ba-a221-cc79bfe9edc2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/32c4bffe-17d4-47bd-ac76-2b0b6f31dd62> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/32c4bffe-17d4-47bd-ac76-2b0b6f31dd62> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/32c4bffe-17d4-47bd-ac76-2b0b6f31dd62> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Extend the supersede/retract lifecycle beyond ArchitecturalDecision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/32c4bffe-17d4-47bd-ac76-2b0b6f31dd62> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/32c4bffe-17d4-47bd-ac76-2b0b6f31dd62> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Gap hit while correcting knowledge: supersede_decision rejects any target that is not an ArchitecturalDecision (\"not an ArchitecturalDecision in the project graph\"), and no other tool can set a Requirement/Constraint/Lesson to superseded or deprecated. So non-AD knowledge cannot be retired or corrected through the lifecycle — when such a record turns out wrong, the only options are leaving an active contradiction or editing the store out-of-band. Concretely, Requirement f1ccd65b and Constraint 0c2106ab both contradict MOOSE's deliberate no-instance-indexing design and SHOULD be retired, but cannot be. The read path (relevant_context) already hides superseded/deprecated for ALL kinds, so only the WRITE side is missing. Fix: extend supersede_decision (or add a retract/set-status tool) to operate on any knowledge class — link new -supersedes-> old with a linked Rationale and mark the old record superseded, preserving history. Directly relates to Requirement b5b101dd (detect/surface/supersede contradictory entries). Until then, contradictions are surfaced (via the correcting Lesson 89dc91bd) but not retired." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/32c4bffe-17d4-47bd-ac76-2b0b6f31dd62> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/32c4bffe-17d4-47bd-ac76-2b0b6f31dd62> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-18T03:59:43.397895Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/32c4bffe-17d4-47bd-ac76-2b0b6f31dd62> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Extend the supersede/retract lifecycle beyond ArchitecturalDecision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/350c7f2e-61bd-49e4-b7cd-2fdd3f51f521> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/350c7f2e-61bd-49e4-b7cd-2fdd3f51f521> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MOOSEDev v3: standalone neurosymbolic coding agent, not an MCP sidecar" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/350c7f2e-61bd-49e4-b7cd-2fdd3f51f521> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/350c7f2e-61bd-49e4-b7cd-2fdd3f51f521> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The eventual v3 goal: MOOSEDev evolves from an MCP memory sidecar into a full neurosymbolic coding agent in its own right — owning the agent loop, with the symbolic layer (project KG of intent + an AST/code-structure graph as world model + a symbolic planner) as the CONTROLLER and the LLM relegated to a sensor/effector (invariant #1: LLM is a sensor, not the controller). Trajectory: v1 = passive MCP memory sidecar (current); v2 = add AST/code-structure indexing (a structural world-model substrate) plus an active-agency layer; v3 = MOOSEDev IS the coding agent, no longer parasitic on a host agent (Claude Code / Cursor / Codex) for code navigation or control flow. Differentiator vs pure-LLM agents: symbolic, auditable control grounded in typed memory + a verifiable code graph, rather than LLM-as-controller. This is the terminus of the 'active memory participant, not passive tool' direction (AD 145af7e9) — the active-agency layer eventually absorbs the whole loop." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/350c7f2e-61bd-49e4-b7cd-2fdd3f51f521> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/350c7f2e-61bd-49e4-b7cd-2fdd3f51f521> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-23T01:53:29.896196Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/350c7f2e-61bd-49e4-b7cd-2fdd3f51f521> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "MOOSEDev v3: standalone neurosymbolic coding agent, not an MCP sidecar" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/4ab93555-0d8d-4bb5-abf5-ce3241f2be90> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
